WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:36.828
JUDGE: Dominic Toretto.

2
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:41.708
You are hereby sentenced
to serve 25 years to life

3
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.712
at the Lompoc Maximum Security
Prison system

4
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:48.798
without the possibility
of early parole.

5
00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:36.345
(TIRES SQUEALING)

6
00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:04.457
Here's what we know so far.

7
00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:08.044
This is all the aftermath
of a daring,
daylight breakout.

8
00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.213
There were 26 high-risk
inmates being transferred...

9
00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:12.882
A daring midday breakout
where everyone onboard
has been accounted for,

10
00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.675
except for one,
Dominic Toretto.

11
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:15.760
Police have
just released the identity

12
00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:18.304
of the man they believe
to have orchestrated
the shocking escape

13
00:02:18.388 --> 00:02:21.057
that amazingly resulted
in no fatalities
this afternoon.

14
00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.018
He is former federal agent,
Brian O'Conner.

15
00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:27.063
A fierce manhunt is underway
for three fugitives tonight.

16
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.982
Multiple federal
and local agencies
have joined forces

17
00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.651
in the search
for Dominic Toretto

18
00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:34.987
and his accomplices
Brian O'Conner
and Mia Toretto.

19
00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.740
But despite every eye
in the country
looking for them

20
00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:41.452
where Toretto
and O'Conner are now
is anyone's guess.

21
00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.572
It's got to be it, right?

22
00:04:06.747 --> 00:04:08.664
(WALKIE TALKIE BEEPING)
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

23
00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:15.296
(GUNS COCKING)

24
00:04:23.847 --> 00:04:24.931
Let's get out of here.
VINCE: Whoa, whoa!

25
00:04:25.015 --> 00:04:26.098
(VINCE SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

26
00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:27.183
Easy, friends.

27
00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.517
She's with me.

28
00:04:30.354 --> 00:04:32.104
(LAUGHING)
Mia.

29
00:04:33.065 --> 00:04:34.690
Vince.

30
00:04:39.363 --> 00:04:40.363
Buster.

31
00:04:42.366 --> 00:04:43.866
Come on.

32
00:04:45.535 --> 00:04:46.786
Dom here yet?

33
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.120
No.

34
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:49.872
When was the last time
you heard from him?

35
00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:53.042
A couple of weeks ago.
Up in Ecuador somewhere.

36
00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.630
VINCE: How does it feel?
What's that?

37
00:04:59.216 --> 00:05:01.550
To be on the other side
of a wanted poster?

38
00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:04.804
He'll show up.

39
00:05:04.888 --> 00:05:06.097
Yeah.

40
00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.312
Dom's?

41
00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:16.107
Yeah.

42
00:05:18.485 --> 00:05:19.527
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

43
00:05:19.611 --> 00:05:20.695
Time for bed little one.

44
00:05:20.779 --> 00:05:22.321
Can I bring him?

45
00:05:22.406 --> 00:05:24.365
Of course.

46
00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:25.449
MIA: Aw.

47
00:05:27.577 --> 00:05:28.744
Good night.

48
00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:31.580
(BABY CRYING)

49
00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:48.431
Excuse me, sorry.

50
00:05:54.438 --> 00:05:56.188
Why Rio, Vince?

51
00:05:57.566 --> 00:05:58.566
(SIGHS)

52
00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:02.611
You mean after you
screwed everything up in LA?

53
00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:07.867
Ended up free-falling
through South America,
you know,

54
00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:11.078
hitting every hellhole
on the way down.

55
00:06:11.163 --> 00:06:14.623
Would have kept
on going if not for Rosa.

56
00:06:31.141 --> 00:06:32.224
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

57
00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:33.309
Does he know?

58
00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.947
So, listen.

59
00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:50.242
There is a job coming up.

60
00:06:50.327 --> 00:06:52.244
I was hoping Dom
was going to be here by now

61
00:06:52.329 --> 00:06:55.831
but this one is clean enough
we can do it without him.

62
00:06:56.625 --> 00:07:01.128
It's a good gig.
Couple of high-end cars,
easy targets.

63
00:07:02.172 --> 00:07:05.174
Guy I know is putting
together a team
to swipe them.

64
00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:07.551
Just need a few more
willing bodies.

65
00:07:07.636 --> 00:07:09.428
I don't know.

66
00:07:09.513 --> 00:07:12.181
Look, the way the car
scene is down here

67
00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:15.226
we can unload them quick
and get top dollar.

68
00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.353
It's easy money.

69
00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:19.688
And from where I'm sitting,

70
00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.943
it looks like you both
could use the payday.

71
00:07:36.915 --> 00:07:37.915
(ENGINE REVVING)

72
00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:04.650
What are you reading?

73
00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.610
Travel guide.

74
00:08:07.195 --> 00:08:08.237
Yeah?

75
00:08:12.159 --> 00:08:13.617
Tokyo.

76
00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:16.453
Moscow.

77
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Goa.

78
00:08:21.084 --> 00:08:22.751
You want to know
what all of these places
have in common?

79
00:08:23.086 --> 00:08:24.086
Huh?

80
00:08:24.921 --> 00:08:26.422
No extradition.

81
00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:42.897
Here we go.

82
00:08:57.454 --> 00:08:58.454
(MACHINE BEEPING)

83
00:08:59.289 --> 00:09:01.165
Excuse me, buddy.

84
00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:17.056
Okay.

85
00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:41.997
Hey, we've found them.

86
00:09:42.207 --> 00:09:43.832
Yeah, second-to-the-last
freighter.

87
00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:55.844
What is it?

88
00:09:55.929 --> 00:09:59.556
DEA tags. These cars
have been seized.

89
00:10:41.224 --> 00:10:42.516
Look who showed up.

90
00:10:43.393 --> 00:10:46.103
God, I'm so happy you're okay.

91
00:10:49.232 --> 00:10:50.607
I thought I told you
to lay low.

92
00:10:50.692 --> 00:10:53.235
Been running on fumes.
Had to make a call.

93
00:10:53.695 --> 00:10:56.613
Hey! Quit talking.
We only got
the two-minute window.

94
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.074
Let's go, Vince.

95
00:11:00.535 --> 00:11:01.535
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

96
00:11:01.619 --> 00:11:02.661
I'm taking the GT40.

97
00:11:39.616 --> 00:11:40.783
Ladies first.

98
00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:47.956
Hey!

99
00:11:49.542 --> 00:11:50.542
MIA: Hey!

100
00:11:50.627 --> 00:11:51.627
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

101
00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:52.753
This car suits me better.

102
00:12:00.303 --> 00:12:02.096
See you, baby.

103
00:12:08.478 --> 00:12:10.229
It's okay...
we're all going
to the same place.

104
00:12:10.313 --> 00:12:12.064
We'll get the car there.

105
00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.406
Change of plans.
Wait for my call.

106
00:12:23.868 --> 00:12:24.910
Let's go!

107
00:12:42.345 --> 00:12:43.387
Where is she going?

108
00:12:45.056 --> 00:12:46.849
Where is she going?
Hey!

109
00:12:48.351 --> 00:12:49.435
Hey!

110
00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:57.484
We're being robbed!
Whatever happens,
don't stop the train!

111
00:12:57.569 --> 00:12:58.610
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

112
00:12:58.695 --> 00:12:59.778
Go after the girl!

113
00:13:00.488 --> 00:13:01.488
Hurry up!

114
00:13:31.519 --> 00:13:34.104
Access card!
Get the access card!

115
00:14:02.759 --> 00:14:03.759
(GRUNTING)

116
00:14:19.817 --> 00:14:20.817
(YELLING)

117
00:14:30.036 --> 00:14:31.036
(SCREAMING)

118
00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:47.970
Shit.

119
00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:50.722
(GRUNTING)

120
00:15:12.829 --> 00:15:14.955
Bridge! There is a bridge!

121
00:15:28.678 --> 00:15:29.678
(ENGINE REVVING)

122
00:15:30.179 --> 00:15:31.638
Luggage car is clear.

123
00:15:38.313 --> 00:15:39.688
Freeze!

124
00:16:39.707 --> 00:16:41.083
Oh, shit!

125
00:17:10.154 --> 00:17:11.154
(COUGHING)

126
00:17:11.698 --> 00:17:13.615
You had to make a call, huh?

127
00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.410
Shitty call, O'Conner.

128
00:17:16.786 --> 00:17:18.537
Shitty call.

129
00:17:20.957 --> 00:17:21.957
(TIRES SCREECHING)

130
00:17:38.474 --> 00:17:41.184
You two stirred up
quite a bit of trouble today.

131
00:17:42.395 --> 00:17:44.396
Three of my men dead.

132
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.857
Three DEA agents
along with them.

133
00:17:47.442 --> 00:17:49.443
Of course,
this is business

134
00:17:49.527 --> 00:17:52.070
and sometimes
things go astray.

135
00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:55.532
All I care about is the car.

136
00:17:55.616 --> 00:17:57.868
Tell me where it is,
and I'll let you go.

137
00:18:00.663 --> 00:18:03.749
BRIAN: This roofing plastic
says you're full of shit.
(REYES LAUGHING)

138
00:18:04.917 --> 00:18:08.295
I don't know how you guys
do business in your part
of the world,

139
00:18:08.379 --> 00:18:09.421
but here in Rio,

140
00:18:10.047 --> 00:18:13.133
I like it when all parties
know what they're up against.

141
00:18:13.217 --> 00:18:14.676
DOM: That's funny.

142
00:18:14.761 --> 00:18:17.304
Because it goes both ways.

143
00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.140
You know,

144
00:18:23.227 --> 00:18:25.812
I hear your sister
is very beautiful.

145
00:18:27.899 --> 00:18:29.691
Wherever she hides

146
00:18:31.068 --> 00:18:32.360
I will find her.

147
00:19:04.727 --> 00:19:05.727
(SHOUTING)

148
00:19:08.731 --> 00:19:09.731
(GRUNTING)

149
00:19:16.531 --> 00:19:18.031
(NEWSCASTER SPEAKING
PORTUGUESE)

150
00:19:18.115 --> 00:19:23.161
The American fugitives
killed three DEA agents
during a train robbery...

151
00:19:23.246 --> 00:19:26.164
...Police warn
they are armed and
extremely dangerous.

152
00:19:26.249 --> 00:19:29.668
Anyone with information
should contact law
enforcement immediately...

153
00:19:29.752 --> 00:19:30.752
(DOOR OPENING)

154
00:19:40.555 --> 00:19:42.013
BRIAN: Mia?

155
00:19:42.932 --> 00:19:43.932
Hey.

156
00:19:46.727 --> 00:19:48.019
You okay?

157
00:19:48.104 --> 00:19:50.021
Yeah, you all right?

158
00:19:52.567 --> 00:19:53.608
Hey.

159
00:19:59.323 --> 00:20:01.241
Hey, yeah.

160
00:20:02.493 --> 00:20:03.785
Just like a Toretto.

161
00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:06.830
Where's Vince?

162
00:20:07.498 --> 00:20:08.748
That's a good question.

163
00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:11.793
He'll be here.

164
00:20:11.878 --> 00:20:13.003
Guys, we're all over
the news.

165
00:20:13.087 --> 00:20:16.464
They're blaming us
for the killing of those
DEA agents on the train.

166
00:20:16.549 --> 00:20:19.593
Which means we just jumped
to the top of the wanted list.

167
00:20:19.677 --> 00:20:22.220
The feds have got
to show everyone
their agents are off limits

168
00:20:22.763 --> 00:20:25.098
and they're going to send
their best guys. We got
to get out of here.

169
00:20:25.433 --> 00:20:28.435
One thing we know for sure

170
00:20:29.896 --> 00:20:31.521
is that they wanted this car.

171
00:20:33.357 --> 00:20:34.441
Because something is in it.

172
00:20:34.525 --> 00:20:38.194
If we find out what it is,
we'll know what we're
up against.

173
00:20:55.546 --> 00:20:58.340
HOBBS: All right, listen up!
The men we're after
are professional runners.

174
00:20:58.424 --> 00:21:01.259
They like speed and are
guaranteed to go down
the hardest possible way

175
00:21:01.344 --> 00:21:02.719
so make sure you got
your funderwear on.

176
00:21:02.803 --> 00:21:05.680
We find them, we take them
as a team, and we bring
them back.

177
00:21:05.765 --> 00:21:10.268
And above all else,
we don't ever, ever let
them get into cars.

178
00:21:10.353 --> 00:21:12.938
Crime scene is 10 hours old
and counting, men.
Let's go hunting.

179
00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.194
Agente Hobbs!
Chief of Police,
João Alemeida.

180
00:21:19.278 --> 00:21:20.445
Luke.

181
00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:23.740
Sorry to hear about
the loss of your men.

182
00:21:23.824 --> 00:21:25.867
Is all this really necessary
to apprehend two men?

183
00:21:25.952 --> 00:21:27.494
Let me tell you something
about these two men.

184
00:21:27.578 --> 00:21:30.080
One is a former federal
officer, been in deep cover
for five years.

185
00:21:30.164 --> 00:21:31.998
He knows every way
you're going to come
for him.

186
00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:35.168
The other one is
a professional criminal,
escaped prison twice,

187
00:21:35.252 --> 00:21:37.796
spent half his life
on the run avoiding
folks like you.

188
00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.715
Well, if there's anything
we can do to help the DSS...

189
00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.842
Two things.
One, I need a translator.

190
00:21:42.927 --> 00:21:44.427
We have plenty
in the public relations
department.

191
00:21:44.512 --> 00:21:46.304
Elena Neves.

192
00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.265
A patrol officer?
You heard me.

193
00:21:50.059 --> 00:21:52.227
But why?
We have many
more experienced people.

194
00:21:52.311 --> 00:21:54.312
I like her smile.

195
00:21:54.397 --> 00:21:56.314
What's the second thing?

196
00:21:57.566 --> 00:22:00.276
Stay the fuck out of my way.

197
00:22:02.697 --> 00:22:03.697
(DRILLING)

198
00:22:10.621 --> 00:22:12.163
Brian.
Hm?

199
00:22:13.624 --> 00:22:15.041
I have something
I have to tell you.

200
00:22:15.209 --> 00:22:16.793
(DOOR OPENING)
VINCE: God damn.

201
00:22:17.586 --> 00:22:18.670
What a mess!

202
00:22:20.464 --> 00:22:22.132
Where you been, man?

203
00:22:22.758 --> 00:22:23.758
(CHUCKLING)

204
00:22:24.885 --> 00:22:26.761
You better check that tone.

205
00:22:26.846 --> 00:22:28.680
And you just better answer
the goddamn question.

206
00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:30.265
Stop it!
Both of you.

207
00:22:33.686 --> 00:22:34.728
Where were you, Vince?

208
00:22:36.022 --> 00:22:38.940
Guys all over
the favelas asking
about you.

209
00:22:39.025 --> 00:22:41.651
Couldn't get out of there
without leading them
straight to you.

210
00:22:41.736 --> 00:22:42.819
Had to wait them out.

211
00:22:42.903 --> 00:22:44.612
That is such horseshit.

212
00:22:44.739 --> 00:22:46.781
(SHOUTING) That was your job,
and those were your guys!
Hey!

213
00:22:46.866 --> 00:22:48.450
Hey! Enough, O'Conner!

214
00:22:48.534 --> 00:22:50.326
If he said he didn't do it,
he didn't do it.

215
00:22:50.411 --> 00:22:51.494
Go walk it off.

216
00:23:06.635 --> 00:23:10.180
REYES: Look, I would love
to expand my operations
into your countries

217
00:23:10.514 --> 00:23:14.267
but, quite frankly,
your business methods
are too violent.

218
00:23:15.352 --> 00:23:17.604
Let me tell you a true story.

219
00:23:17.813 --> 00:23:22.108
Five hundred years ago,
the Portuguese
and the Spanish came here,

220
00:23:22.193 --> 00:23:25.653
each trying to get the country
from their natives.

221
00:23:27.907 --> 00:23:32.368
The Spaniards arrived,
guns blazing, determined
to prove who was boss.

222
00:23:34.705 --> 00:23:37.999
The natives killed
every single Spaniard.

223
00:23:39.877 --> 00:23:43.838
Personally, I prefer
the methods of the Portuguese.

224
00:23:45.508 --> 00:23:47.092
They came bearing gifts.

225
00:23:47.176 --> 00:23:49.469
Mirrors, scissors, trinkets.

226
00:23:50.346 --> 00:23:54.015
Things that the natives
couldn't get on their own,

227
00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:57.352
but to continue receiving
them, they had to work
for the Portuguese.

228
00:23:58.521 --> 00:24:01.898
And that's why
all Brazilians speak
Portuguese today.

229
00:24:02.733 --> 00:24:06.444
Now, if you dominate
the people with violence,

230
00:24:07.363 --> 00:24:10.782
they will eventually
fight back because
they have nothing to lose.

231
00:24:11.408 --> 00:24:13.493
And that's the key.

232
00:24:13.577 --> 00:24:17.372
I go into the favelas
and give them
something to lose.

233
00:24:18.374 --> 00:24:20.208
Electricity, running water,

234
00:24:20.292 --> 00:24:22.418
school rooms for their kids.

235
00:24:24.004 --> 00:24:26.881
And for that taste
of a better life,

236
00:24:28.425 --> 00:24:30.385
I own them.

237
00:24:31.554 --> 00:24:32.595
Gentlemen.

238
00:24:34.557 --> 00:24:35.557
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

239
00:24:36.100 --> 00:24:37.183
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

240
00:24:37.268 --> 00:24:38.434
I apologize for
the interruption.

241
00:24:38.978 --> 00:24:41.521
Señor Reyes,
may I speak with you?

242
00:24:41.605 --> 00:24:44.107
We've found them.

243
00:24:45.568 --> 00:24:47.777
Pardon me, gentlemen.

244
00:25:02.751 --> 00:25:04.919
DOM: Almost wish
I didn't see that.

245
00:25:08.257 --> 00:25:10.175
Almost.

246
00:25:10.259 --> 00:25:12.302
Wait, Dom.

247
00:25:12.928 --> 00:25:14.554
Mia was on that train.

248
00:25:14.638 --> 00:25:16.264
(SHOUTING)
My sister!

249
00:25:16.974 --> 00:25:19.517
I didn't know.
I wouldn't do
anything to hurt her.

250
00:25:19.602 --> 00:25:21.936
You set up the deal!

251
00:25:22.396 --> 00:25:24.647
I thought the job
was for the cars.

252
00:25:25.107 --> 00:25:26.858
I didn't know.

253
00:25:26.942 --> 00:25:28.401
All they want is the chip.

254
00:25:30.404 --> 00:25:32.113
Damn!

255
00:25:32.781 --> 00:25:34.407
You should've come clean.

256
00:25:34.491 --> 00:25:36.075
What's going on out here?

257
00:25:36.785 --> 00:25:38.161
Nothing.

258
00:25:38.287 --> 00:25:41.706
Please, Dom, just let
me have the chip.
I can take this to them.

259
00:25:41.957 --> 00:25:43.958
They'll give it to Reyes
and set things right.

260
00:25:44.960 --> 00:25:46.044
Get out.

261
00:25:49.298 --> 00:25:50.924
What?

262
00:25:51.008 --> 00:25:52.050
Get out!

263
00:25:59.642 --> 00:26:02.227
You never listen to me.

264
00:26:02.311 --> 00:26:05.980
Not when I told you
he was a cop, and not now.

265
00:26:06.982 --> 00:26:10.777
You never trust me
and look where it's gotten us.

266
00:26:11.403 --> 00:26:13.154
Look at our family now.

267
00:26:13.656 --> 00:26:18.284
I can't go home!
Your sister is stuck
in this life!

268
00:26:19.161 --> 00:26:20.328
Where's Letty, Dom?

269
00:26:22.831 --> 00:26:23.831
Where's Letty?

270
00:26:48.315 --> 00:26:49.774
Plasma cutter.

271
00:26:49.858 --> 00:26:53.111
Wilkes, I want a list
of every place within 50 miles

272
00:26:53.195 --> 00:26:54.946
that distributes
compressed gas tanks.

273
00:26:55.030 --> 00:26:57.156
Pass me that manifest.

274
00:27:03.789 --> 00:27:05.832
Officer Neves.
Been waiting for you.

275
00:27:06.125 --> 00:27:08.293
You asked for me?
I did.

276
00:27:08.544 --> 00:27:10.044
May I ask why?

277
00:27:11.130 --> 00:27:12.547
My smile
is not that great.

278
00:27:16.051 --> 00:27:18.678
Your husband was
an officer who was
gunned down in the favela.

279
00:27:18.762 --> 00:27:20.638
Six months later,
you upped and joined
the force.

280
00:27:20.723 --> 00:27:21.973
You're motivated.

281
00:27:22.850 --> 00:27:25.810
Plus, I figure you're
the only one in Rio
who can't be bought.

282
00:27:25.894 --> 00:27:27.312
Am I right?

283
00:27:28.605 --> 00:27:30.732
Yes.
Of course I am.

284
00:27:30.816 --> 00:27:31.983
Good news, bad news.

285
00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:33.735
You know I like
my dessert first.

286
00:27:33.819 --> 00:27:35.778
Back-checked
the rail line like you asked.

287
00:27:35.863 --> 00:27:37.864
Found a couple of spots
where they unloaded the cars.

288
00:27:38.198 --> 00:27:39.657
One set of tracks
headed west

289
00:27:39.742 --> 00:27:42.410
until it hit the main highway,
then disappeared.

290
00:27:42.494 --> 00:27:43.786
But another set
of tracks headed east.

291
00:27:43.871 --> 00:27:46.247
A 107-inch wheelbase,
eight-and-a-half-inch tread.

292
00:27:46.707 --> 00:27:48.916
The GT40 that was missing
from the manifest.

293
00:27:49.001 --> 00:27:50.585
Followed the trail
a couple of miles.

294
00:27:50.669 --> 00:27:51.878
Pretty easy in this scrub.

295
00:27:52.171 --> 00:27:53.713
Can't move without
leaving a sign.

296
00:27:53.797 --> 00:27:55.256
Give me the damn veggies.

297
00:27:55.341 --> 00:27:58.634
The ground rolls into
a hardpack and we lost
that track, too.

298
00:27:59.970 --> 00:28:01.471
Not necessarily.

299
00:28:01.972 --> 00:28:04.974
That road heads up
through the hills
into the favelas.

300
00:28:05.059 --> 00:28:07.393
Couple of years ago,
it was washed out by a storm.

301
00:28:07.770 --> 00:28:09.854
It's all dirt a mile
from where you were.

302
00:28:09.938 --> 00:28:13.107
If they headed that way,
we'll pick up
their tracks there.

303
00:28:13.192 --> 00:28:15.443
You come prepared.

304
00:28:15.527 --> 00:28:16.986
I'm motivated.

305
00:28:17.696 --> 00:28:18.738
HOBBS: All right, then.

306
00:28:19.448 --> 00:28:21.532
Let's find ourselves a car.

307
00:28:50.771 --> 00:28:51.771
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

308
00:28:52.147 --> 00:28:53.189
What do you think?

309
00:28:53.273 --> 00:28:55.691
Well, it's definitely
a custom chip.

310
00:28:56.276 --> 00:28:59.404
Look at all these side menus
here for data entry.

311
00:28:59.488 --> 00:29:01.322
Let's check this one.

312
00:29:06.036 --> 00:29:07.453
Look at that.

313
00:29:07.538 --> 00:29:09.956
Same building,
same order every week.

314
00:29:10.040 --> 00:29:11.874
It's a delivery schedule.

315
00:29:33.021 --> 00:29:34.021
What's this?

316
00:29:35.441 --> 00:29:36.441
Drugs?

317
00:29:36.525 --> 00:29:39.444
No. That's a dealer pack.

318
00:29:39.528 --> 00:29:41.446
See, most major players,
they weigh their money

319
00:29:41.530 --> 00:29:43.406
so they don't have
to constantly count it.

320
00:29:43.490 --> 00:29:44.824
Right there,
that's 49 kilos.

321
00:29:44.908 --> 00:29:46.868
49 kilos is a million
in twenties.

322
00:29:47.536 --> 00:29:50.037
You're saying each one
of these shipments
is worth 10 million dollars?

323
00:29:50.122 --> 00:29:51.164
Yeah.

324
00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:54.125
(GUN COCKING)

325
00:30:14.188 --> 00:30:16.063
I thought so.

326
00:30:18.484 --> 00:30:20.109
So what is that?

327
00:30:20.194 --> 00:30:22.820
A 100-million plus
in cash houses?

328
00:30:22.905 --> 00:30:24.780
That's how he keeps it
off the grid.

329
00:30:27.409 --> 00:30:29.911
I think it's safe to say
that Reyes is smart
to want this back.

330
00:30:29.995 --> 00:30:32.747
It's his whole network
right there, just laid
out on a chip.

331
00:30:32.831 --> 00:30:33.831
(GLASS TINKLING)

332
00:30:49.097 --> 00:30:50.097
(YELLING)

333
00:30:56.271 --> 00:30:57.605
Wilkes, Fusco,
up the middle.

334
00:30:57.689 --> 00:30:59.357
Mac, Chato,
flank north.

335
00:30:59.441 --> 00:31:01.108
What about me?

336
00:31:01.193 --> 00:31:02.193
Stay here.

337
00:31:05.822 --> 00:31:06.822
(YELLING)

338
00:31:11.328 --> 00:31:12.370
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

339
00:31:12.454 --> 00:31:13.496
Go that way!

340
00:31:13.580 --> 00:31:14.956
The other two
went over the wall!

341
00:31:40.983 --> 00:31:41.983
(BOTH GRUNTING)

342
00:31:58.333 --> 00:31:59.417
Come on, go! Go!

343
00:32:12.681 --> 00:32:13.681
(YELLING)

344
00:32:56.141 --> 00:32:57.141
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

345
00:32:57.684 --> 00:32:59.352
Get on the ground.

346
00:33:00.187 --> 00:33:02.438
I got Toretto.
Four blocks north of your...

347
00:33:07.944 --> 00:33:09.737
They already know
who you are.

348
00:33:09.863 --> 00:33:10.863
(YELLING IN PORTUGUESE)

349
00:33:31.593 --> 00:33:32.593
(GASPS)

350
00:33:41.728 --> 00:33:43.145
Let's go.

351
00:33:53.615 --> 00:33:54.615
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

352
00:34:28.608 --> 00:34:30.025
You okay here?

353
00:34:30.110 --> 00:34:33.779
Yeah. I'm good.
Thank you.

354
00:35:08.523 --> 00:35:11.317
They're going to be looking
for the three of us
together now.

355
00:35:11.485 --> 00:35:14.111
We need to split up.

356
00:35:14.196 --> 00:35:17.031
You and Mia head south,
I'll lead them away.

357
00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:18.115
No.

358
00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:20.493
Dom is right.

359
00:35:20.577 --> 00:35:22.286
Look how lucky we just got.
What happens next time?

360
00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:23.412
We have no choice
but to split up.

361
00:35:23.497 --> 00:35:24.747
I'm pregnant.

362
00:35:29.586 --> 00:35:31.086
I already lost
my family once.

363
00:35:33.173 --> 00:35:35.716
I'm not going through
that again.

364
00:35:36.176 --> 00:35:38.385
Are you kidding me?
No.

365
00:35:43.642 --> 00:35:46.268
I'm not going
anywhere. Okay?

366
00:35:48.647 --> 00:35:49.730
Dom?

367
00:35:50.732 --> 00:35:52.775
Promise me
we stick together.

368
00:36:00.534 --> 00:36:02.409
I promise.

369
00:36:06.998 --> 00:36:09.458
Our family
just got bigger.

370
00:36:27.561 --> 00:36:29.311
Something
doesn't add up.

371
00:36:29.771 --> 00:36:31.272
Toretto and O'Conner.

372
00:36:31.773 --> 00:36:36.360
They stay when they're
supposed to run, they steal
gas then give it away?

373
00:36:36.528 --> 00:36:38.070
Now they're killing
federal agents?

374
00:36:39.406 --> 00:36:40.865
It doesn't make any sense.

375
00:36:40.949 --> 00:36:42.741
Here's what makes sense.

376
00:36:47.414 --> 00:36:48.998
All these guys are
is names on a list.

377
00:36:49.082 --> 00:36:50.499
They come up,
we take them down.

378
00:36:50.584 --> 00:36:53.085
Not a phone call more,
not a bullet less.

379
00:36:53.169 --> 00:36:54.879
Wilkes, we get anything?

380
00:36:55.255 --> 00:36:56.630
Standard forensics.

381
00:36:56.715 --> 00:36:58.507
Shoe prints.
Hair and fiber.

382
00:36:58.592 --> 00:36:59.717
Prints are all over the car.

383
00:36:59.801 --> 00:37:00.885
Anything else?

384
00:37:00.969 --> 00:37:03.262
Yeah, we tracked the owner
off the vehicle ID.

385
00:37:03.346 --> 00:37:04.805
There are a couple
of shell companies
in between,

386
00:37:04.890 --> 00:37:07.349
but we finally
traced it back
to a corporation

387
00:37:07.434 --> 00:37:10.102
owned by an investor
down here named
Hernan Reyes.

388
00:37:10.186 --> 00:37:11.186
Investor?

389
00:37:12.397 --> 00:37:15.649
If there's anything
illegal happening in Rio,
Reyes is involved.

390
00:37:15.734 --> 00:37:17.359
Okay, then so are we.

391
00:37:17.444 --> 00:37:19.653
If he could get us
any closer to our guys,
I want everything on him.

392
00:37:19.738 --> 00:37:21.071
Chato, you're
on the roof.

393
00:37:21.156 --> 00:37:23.449
I want you on overwatch
in case somebody comes
back for something.

394
00:37:23.533 --> 00:37:25.910
Mac, give me a cross-check
on Reyes, full specs.

395
00:37:25.994 --> 00:37:28.203
If he goes to the john,
I want to know how
many times he shakes it.

396
00:37:28.288 --> 00:37:30.664
You got it, boss.
Wilkes, Fusco!

397
00:37:31.374 --> 00:37:33.250
Let's put all this
mess back together.

398
00:37:35.629 --> 00:37:37.296
That's going to take a while.

399
00:37:37.380 --> 00:37:38.631
Then you better get started.

400
00:37:39.049 --> 00:37:40.633
They were taking
this car apart for a reason.

401
00:37:40.717 --> 00:37:42.509
Let's put it back together
and find out what's missing.

402
00:37:42.677 --> 00:37:43.677
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

403
00:38:10.205 --> 00:38:13.540
Hey, Dom,
what do you remember
about your father?

404
00:38:16.002 --> 00:38:17.711
My father.

405
00:38:21.883 --> 00:38:24.134
He used to...

406
00:38:24.803 --> 00:38:28.180
He used to have a barbecue
every Sunday after church.

407
00:38:28.848 --> 00:38:31.225
For anybody
in the neighborhood.

408
00:38:32.143 --> 00:38:34.520
If you didn't go to church,
you didn't get any barbecue.

409
00:38:36.356 --> 00:38:40.150
Every single day he was
in the shop, and every
single night,

410
00:38:40.235 --> 00:38:45.239
he was at the kitchen table
with Mia, helping her
with her homework.

411
00:38:46.658 --> 00:38:49.284
Even after she went to sleep,

412
00:38:49.369 --> 00:38:52.413
he'd stay up
for a few more hours

413
00:38:52.497 --> 00:38:56.458
so he could learn
the next chapter
and help her the next day.

414
00:38:57.711 --> 00:38:59.420
I remember everything
about my father.

415
00:39:01.006 --> 00:39:02.297
Everything.

416
00:39:03.425 --> 00:39:04.758
That's just it.

417
00:39:05.135 --> 00:39:06.635
I don't remember shit
about my dad.

418
00:39:10.348 --> 00:39:11.807
I don't remember
him yelling.

419
00:39:11.891 --> 00:39:13.350
I don't remember
him smiling.

420
00:39:15.395 --> 00:39:17.938
To be honest with you,
I don't even remember
what the hell he looked like.

421
00:39:20.108 --> 00:39:22.234
I don't remember.
He just...

422
00:39:24.070 --> 00:39:25.446
He was just never there.

423
00:39:27.657 --> 00:39:29.783
You ain't going
to be like that, Brian.

424
00:39:46.426 --> 00:39:48.552
We can't keep
running, Dom.

425
00:39:50.221 --> 00:39:51.847
We got to get out.

426
00:39:51.931 --> 00:39:53.849
We got to get out now.

427
00:39:55.060 --> 00:39:56.393
You're right.

428
00:40:07.989 --> 00:40:09.656
Here's how we're
going to do it.

429
00:40:13.870 --> 00:40:15.079
We're going to use this.

430
00:40:16.247 --> 00:40:18.082
We're going do one last job.

431
00:40:18.583 --> 00:40:20.876
We're going to take
all of Reyes' money.

432
00:40:21.169 --> 00:40:22.753
Every dime of it,

433
00:40:23.671 --> 00:40:25.339
and disappear.

434
00:40:28.968 --> 00:40:29.968
Forever.

435
00:40:31.513 --> 00:40:32.679
New passports.

436
00:40:32.764 --> 00:40:35.182
New lives
with no more looking
over our shoulder.

437
00:40:35.266 --> 00:40:36.934
And we're just going
to buy our freedom.

438
00:40:37.018 --> 00:40:38.060
That's right.

439
00:40:38.144 --> 00:40:39.728
You realize we're
talking about going
up against

440
00:40:39.813 --> 00:40:41.146
the most powerful guy
in all of Rio?

441
00:40:41.439 --> 00:40:42.898
Yes, we are.

442
00:40:44.317 --> 00:40:46.235
Then we're going
to need a team.

443
00:40:52.826 --> 00:40:55.202
Let's run through
the bases real quick.
Who do we got?

444
00:40:55.286 --> 00:40:56.662
First we're going
to need a chameleon.

445
00:40:58.164 --> 00:41:02.042
Someone who can
blend in anywhere.

446
00:41:03.086 --> 00:41:04.086
What else?

447
00:41:04.170 --> 00:41:05.212
A fast talker.

448
00:41:06.131 --> 00:41:08.632
Someone who can
bullshit their way
out of anything.

449
00:41:09.050 --> 00:41:10.050
I got that.

450
00:41:11.886 --> 00:41:13.470
This guy is going to have
a lot of surveillance.

451
00:41:13.555 --> 00:41:15.264
We're going to need someone
who's good with circuits.

452
00:41:17.433 --> 00:41:20.060
DOM: And with those circuits,
Reyes is going to have walls.

453
00:41:20.145 --> 00:41:22.437
We're going to need guys
to punch through those walls.

454
00:41:24.399 --> 00:41:25.440
MIA: What else?

455
00:41:25.984 --> 00:41:27.734
Utilities and weapons.

456
00:41:27.819 --> 00:41:30.571
Someone who ain't
afraid to throw down.

457
00:41:31.489 --> 00:41:33.490
Someone to back up
every position.

458
00:41:33.575 --> 00:41:35.117
BRIAN: Yeah, what else
do we need?

459
00:41:35.201 --> 00:41:36.827
DOM: Most importantly,

460
00:41:37.912 --> 00:41:40.122
we're going to need
two precision drivers.

461
00:41:40.206 --> 00:41:42.833
Guys that don't crack
under pressure.

462
00:41:42.917 --> 00:41:44.376
Guys that never lose.

463
00:41:45.670 --> 00:41:46.962
You know we got that.

464
00:42:06.482 --> 00:42:07.482
(ENGINE REVVING)

465
00:42:08.276 --> 00:42:09.443
(HIP HOP BEAT PLAYING
ON CAR STEREO)

466
00:42:13.156 --> 00:42:14.156
(MUSIC STOPS)

467
00:42:14.866 --> 00:42:16.867
Aw, hell, no!

468
00:42:17.827 --> 00:42:20.537
I see they really scraped
the bottom of the barrel, huh?

469
00:42:20.622 --> 00:42:22.915
I guess they did,
since your ass is here.

470
00:42:24.667 --> 00:42:27.711
When are you going
to give Martin Luther King
his car back?

471
00:42:27.795 --> 00:42:30.547
As soon as you give
Rick James his jacket back.

472
00:42:31.216 --> 00:42:32.216
(LAUGHING)

473
00:42:33.801 --> 00:42:35.928
What's up, man?
What's up?

474
00:42:47.190 --> 00:42:48.190
Hmm.

475
00:42:48.942 --> 00:42:51.109
Sexy legs,
baby girl.

476
00:42:51.194 --> 00:42:52.402
What time do they open?

477
00:42:53.279 --> 00:42:57.074
They open the same time
as I pull this trigger.

478
00:42:57.617 --> 00:42:59.076
Want me to open them?

479
00:43:01.204 --> 00:43:02.371
(TEGO SPEAKING SPANISH)

480
00:43:02.455 --> 00:43:05.332
I told you the skinny
chick had balls.

481
00:43:05.458 --> 00:43:07.960
Looks like she started
the party without us.

482
00:43:08.544 --> 00:43:11.171
Hey, anybody can talk shit
in Spanish, homie.

483
00:43:11.756 --> 00:43:14.091
What's this guy saying?

484
00:43:14.801 --> 00:43:16.718
Ugly is still ugly in
Spanish or in English.

485
00:43:17.220 --> 00:43:19.888
(BOTH TAUNTING IN SPANISH)

486
00:43:20.014 --> 00:43:22.099
Who are these clowns, man?
Circus clowns.

487
00:43:22.183 --> 00:43:23.183
(ALL CHATTERING ANGRILY)

488
00:43:24.227 --> 00:43:27.229
I thought cockfights
were illegal in Brazil.

489
00:43:27.313 --> 00:43:29.398
I see you all have met.

490
00:43:31.109 --> 00:43:33.193
You know when you called me
to come to Rio

491
00:43:33.278 --> 00:43:36.113
I assumed it would be
for something more
exciting than this.

492
00:43:36.197 --> 00:43:37.197
Look at this guy.

493
00:43:37.282 --> 00:43:39.408
Long time.
I missed you, man.

494
00:43:39.492 --> 00:43:40.575
Good to see you.

495
00:43:40.660 --> 00:43:42.577
Brother.
What's up?

496
00:43:42.662 --> 00:43:44.746
Yo, check this out.
This is Tej.

497
00:43:44.831 --> 00:43:46.748
Best circuit man
on the East Coast.

498
00:43:46.833 --> 00:43:48.333
And this is my boy,
Roman Pearce.

499
00:43:48.668 --> 00:43:50.919
We go way back,
I met this guy in juvie.

500
00:43:51.004 --> 00:43:52.629
I pulled that job
with him in Miami.

501
00:43:52.714 --> 00:43:54.131
I've heard about you.

502
00:43:55.300 --> 00:43:56.800
Nice digs.

503
00:43:56.884 --> 00:43:58.677
Yeah, well,
the Ritz was sold out.

504
00:43:59.220 --> 00:44:00.971
So what's this
all about, Dom?

505
00:44:01.055 --> 00:44:04.391
Yeah, man, why did
you drag us halfway
around the world?

506
00:44:04.475 --> 00:44:06.268
Because we got a job.

507
00:44:07.270 --> 00:44:09.896
All right,
so our target's name
is Hernan Reyes.

508
00:44:09.981 --> 00:44:11.690
And he runs
the drug scene down here.

509
00:44:11.774 --> 00:44:14.318
He's never been busted
because he doesn't
leave a paper trail.

510
00:44:14.402 --> 00:44:16.445
No paper trail
means no banks.

511
00:44:16.529 --> 00:44:18.613
And no banks means
cash houses.

512
00:44:18.698 --> 00:44:21.116
That's right.
Ten of them,
to be exact.

513
00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:23.368
Spread throughout the city.

514
00:44:23.453 --> 00:44:25.287
And we're going
to hit them all.

515
00:44:26.748 --> 00:44:27.748
All of them?

516
00:44:28.166 --> 00:44:29.249
All of them.

517
00:44:29.334 --> 00:44:31.251
That sounds crazy.

518
00:44:31.336 --> 00:44:33.295
You bring us
to a whole other country

519
00:44:33.379 --> 00:44:35.422
so we can rob
the dude who runs it?

520
00:44:36.549 --> 00:44:38.175
I thought this was business.

521
00:44:38.468 --> 00:44:39.760
Sounds personal to me.

522
00:44:40.678 --> 00:44:42.304
Is that what this is?

523
00:44:42.388 --> 00:44:46.183
I got love for y'all,
but personal ain't
good business.

524
00:44:47.810 --> 00:44:50.062
I can't do this, homie.

525
00:44:51.314 --> 00:44:55.442
So what we're talking
about is $100 million.

526
00:44:55.610 --> 00:44:57.569
You say what?

527
00:44:57.653 --> 00:45:01.281
Hundred...
See, sometimes I be
over thinking, man,

528
00:45:01.366 --> 00:45:04.409
and I know we just met,
but you just, kind of,
got to...

529
00:45:04.494 --> 00:45:08.246
That's right, $100 million,
and everything we take,

530
00:45:08.331 --> 00:45:09.748
we split even.

531
00:45:09.832 --> 00:45:11.625
TEJ: That's a little over
$11 million apiece.

532
00:45:12.627 --> 00:45:14.002
I am down.

533
00:45:14.462 --> 00:45:15.504
I'm in.

534
00:45:17.131 --> 00:45:18.548
Eleven million.

535
00:45:18.966 --> 00:45:21.676
Sounds like a whole lot of
vaginal activity to me.

536
00:45:22.136 --> 00:45:24.429
You can't pull off 10 heists
on the same mark.

537
00:45:24.514 --> 00:45:25.597
You just can't.

538
00:45:25.681 --> 00:45:27.224
As soon as we hit
the first one,

539
00:45:27.308 --> 00:45:30.060
they're going to do
everything they can
to protect the rest.

540
00:45:31.062 --> 00:45:32.813
Exactly.

541
00:45:49.747 --> 00:45:50.747
(CASH MACHINES WHIRRING)

542
00:45:53.668 --> 00:45:54.668
(DOORBELL BUZZING)

543
00:46:10.226 --> 00:46:11.309
(GRUNTING)
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

544
00:46:11.394 --> 00:46:12.519
Nobody move!

545
00:46:12.603 --> 00:46:13.812
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

546
00:46:27.702 --> 00:46:28.910
That's all of it.

547
00:46:28.995 --> 00:46:30.203
You a dead man.

548
00:46:30.288 --> 00:46:31.371
You're all dead men!

549
00:46:32.206 --> 00:46:33.707
You don't have
a place to hide.

550
00:46:36.669 --> 00:46:37.711
Who's hiding?

551
00:46:37.795 --> 00:46:39.087
THUG: Are you crazy?

552
00:46:39.172 --> 00:46:40.380
Are you crazy?

553
00:46:40.465 --> 00:46:43.341
Do you know whose house
this is? Whose money
are you stealing?

554
00:46:53.811 --> 00:46:55.228
We ain't stealing it.

555
00:47:04.155 --> 00:47:07.240
You tell your boss
exactly who did this.

556
00:47:08.868 --> 00:47:10.368
Tell him there's more coming.

557
00:47:16.042 --> 00:47:17.042
Voilà.

558
00:47:18.002 --> 00:47:19.002
Turn it over.

559
00:47:22.381 --> 00:47:23.381
(ENGINE STARTING)

560
00:47:25.176 --> 00:47:28.386
She's running on all eight.
Checks out fine.

561
00:47:30.932 --> 00:47:32.849
Keep looking.

562
00:47:33.392 --> 00:47:34.392
(SIGHING)

563
00:47:34.894 --> 00:47:38.438
Boss, if something
was missing, we'd know.

564
00:48:04.048 --> 00:48:07.717
It's a goddamn shame
putting bullshit
like that on a classic.

565
00:48:08.094 --> 00:48:10.136
You may as well slap
neon lights on it.

566
00:48:17.395 --> 00:48:18.395
(BEEPING)

567
00:48:21.399 --> 00:48:23.400
They took the chip.

568
00:48:23.484 --> 00:48:27.237
We got a hit on the police
scanner. Armed robbery at
a house in Leblon.

569
00:48:27.321 --> 00:48:28.738
Address cross-checks
against property

570
00:48:28.823 --> 00:48:30.490
owned by one
of Hernan Reyes' corporations.

571
00:48:30.575 --> 00:48:31.741
All right,
if that's our guys

572
00:48:31.826 --> 00:48:34.411
then whatever was on
that chip led them
directly to that house.

573
00:48:34.495 --> 00:48:35.662
It's them, for sure.

574
00:48:35.746 --> 00:48:37.080
How do you know that?

575
00:48:37.164 --> 00:48:41.459
Because no one else in Rio
is stupid enough to rob Reyes.

576
00:48:54.098 --> 00:48:55.098
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

577
00:48:55.182 --> 00:48:56.266
Explain.

578
00:48:56.350 --> 00:48:58.018
They invaded
the Leblon house.

579
00:48:58.394 --> 00:48:59.728
Who invaded?

580
00:48:59.812 --> 00:49:02.188
The men from the train.

581
00:49:10.531 --> 00:49:12.741
How much did they take?

582
00:49:12.908 --> 00:49:14.701
They didn't
take anything.

583
00:49:14.869 --> 00:49:18.413
They burned it!

584
00:49:18.706 --> 00:49:20.290
They burned my money?

585
00:49:20.374 --> 00:49:23.501
Yes. And said
there's more coming.

586
00:49:28.841 --> 00:49:29.841
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

587
00:49:31.552 --> 00:49:32.594
Okay...

588
00:49:41.228 --> 00:49:43.229
Then this...

589
00:49:45.107 --> 00:49:46.566
...is what
we're going to do.

590
00:49:53.115 --> 00:49:54.741
Clean the houses.

591
00:49:55.034 --> 00:49:59.245
I want that money
under lock and key...

592
00:50:00.706 --> 00:50:01.790
...within an hour.

593
00:50:01.874 --> 00:50:04.084
Understand?

594
00:50:06.295 --> 00:50:07.921
Understood.

595
00:50:26.899 --> 00:50:29.317
Number One
is on the move, man.

596
00:50:43.708 --> 00:50:45.250
ROME: Two is on the move.

597
00:51:09.984 --> 00:51:10.984
I got mine.

598
00:51:32.006 --> 00:51:34.007
I got eyes on Five.

599
00:52:00.701 --> 00:52:04.037
I know y'all said
they were consolidating
the money somewhere, but,

600
00:52:04.371 --> 00:52:07.248
y'all ain't going
to believe this.

601
00:52:16.967 --> 00:52:19.427
Well, this job just got
a lot harder.

602
00:52:20.095 --> 00:52:21.930
If he's moving it
into a police station

603
00:52:22.014 --> 00:52:24.474
he's got some serious
brass in his pocket.

604
00:52:24.558 --> 00:52:25.558
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

605
00:52:25.643 --> 00:52:27.143
Looks like this is going
to be a shorter trip
than I thought...

606
00:52:27.228 --> 00:52:28.436
Hell, yeah,
we can't do this.

607
00:52:28.521 --> 00:52:32.023
"Can't"? You mean,
"shouldn't."

608
00:52:32.983 --> 00:52:35.068
I think this doesn't
change a thing.

609
00:52:38.155 --> 00:52:40.490
I say we stick to the plan.

610
00:52:40.574 --> 00:52:42.242
You say what?

611
00:52:42.326 --> 00:52:43.993
This just went
from Mission: Lmpossible

612
00:52:44.078 --> 00:52:45.954
to Mission:
In-freaking-sanity.

613
00:52:48.165 --> 00:52:49.415
Whatever, man.

614
00:52:49.500 --> 00:52:52.877
I ain't scared, I'm just
letting you all know, going
in that building is crazy.

615
00:52:52.962 --> 00:52:54.379
BRIAN: I got this.

616
00:52:58.008 --> 00:52:59.342
What time
was the robbery?

617
00:52:59.426 --> 00:53:01.261
Around 11:00.

618
00:53:02.805 --> 00:53:04.013
Here we go.

619
00:53:06.183 --> 00:53:07.684
Enhance it.

620
00:53:09.812 --> 00:53:11.229
Their faces are covered.

621
00:53:11.313 --> 00:53:12.438
Run it through FRS.

622
00:53:18.529 --> 00:53:20.154
Well, hello,
you son of a bitch.

623
00:53:23.033 --> 00:53:26.077
Wilkes! Run the photos
of known associates
of Toretto and O'Conner

624
00:53:26.161 --> 00:53:29.038
against customs entries
into Brazil in the last
two weeks.

625
00:53:29.123 --> 00:53:32.292
Check planes, trains,
boats, everything short
of the goddamn space shuttle.

626
00:53:38.632 --> 00:53:41.718
They can change their names
but they can't change
their faces.

627
00:53:41.802 --> 00:53:43.553
Something big
is going down.

628
00:53:45.306 --> 00:53:46.723
That's a 1970 Charger.

629
00:53:46.807 --> 00:53:48.892
Fusco! Upload these specs
into the database.

630
00:53:48.976 --> 00:53:51.269
Have the computer cross-check
it with overhead satellites

631
00:53:51.353 --> 00:53:53.354
every 15 minutes,
the van behind it, too.

632
00:53:53.439 --> 00:53:56.190
If these vehicles move
in the streets of Rio,
I want to know about it.

633
00:54:03.991 --> 00:54:04.991
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

634
00:54:05.075 --> 00:54:06.075
Everything okay?

635
00:54:06.160 --> 00:54:07.201
Everything is okay.

636
00:54:07.286 --> 00:54:09.954
Who is this Hobbs?
This Federal Agent
running around town?

637
00:54:10.205 --> 00:54:11.205
Some American cowboy.

638
00:54:11.957 --> 00:54:12.957
He's handled.

639
00:54:13.208 --> 00:54:14.667
He killed sixteen
of our men.

640
00:54:15.377 --> 00:54:16.586
Handle him better.

641
00:54:16.754 --> 00:54:22.050
Look... He requested
a rookie patrol officer
as his assistant.

642
00:54:24.803 --> 00:54:25.803
They won't be a problem.

643
00:54:54.792 --> 00:54:56.709
It's all here?
Yes.

644
00:54:58.212 --> 00:54:59.963
What about Toretto
and O'Conner?
Where are they?

645
00:55:00.422 --> 00:55:01.422
Nothing yet.

646
00:55:02.466 --> 00:55:04.300
But I have all our
officers searching.

647
00:55:05.135 --> 00:55:06.260
Not good enough.

648
00:55:07.137 --> 00:55:08.554
Put a price
on their heads.

649
00:55:08.722 --> 00:55:10.139
High enough...

650
00:55:10.724 --> 00:55:12.850
...to get every pair
of eyes in the city
searching for them.

651
00:55:20.317 --> 00:55:22.819
The beauty of public offices?

652
00:55:25.739 --> 00:55:26.739
Public records.

653
00:55:27.157 --> 00:55:29.575
This is where he's keeping
the money. The vault
in the evidence room.

654
00:55:30.661 --> 00:55:34.998
Um. Uh, yeah. Can I get
everyone's attention,
right here, for a second?

655
00:55:35.082 --> 00:55:38.751
We're talking about
breaking into
a police station.

656
00:55:38.836 --> 00:55:40.545
Is anyone listening
to those words?

657
00:55:40.629 --> 00:55:42.171
Anybody? Popo?

658
00:55:42.256 --> 00:55:44.841
Five-O. One-time. Pigs.

659
00:55:44.925 --> 00:55:46.217
People we don't like.

660
00:55:46.301 --> 00:55:49.220
You know, police stations
are designed to keep
people in, not out.

661
00:55:49.304 --> 00:55:50.596
That's why it's
a stealth mission.

662
00:55:51.015 --> 00:55:53.725
We'll be in and out
before they even know
we were there.

663
00:55:53.809 --> 00:55:55.351
Well, we'll need
to get eyes in there.

664
00:55:55.436 --> 00:55:57.895
At least to find out
the make and model
of that vault.

665
00:55:58.147 --> 00:56:01.482
So the vault
and then, so...

666
00:56:01.567 --> 00:56:03.026
It's crazy.

667
00:56:03.110 --> 00:56:05.945
Who's supposed
to do all this?

668
00:56:14.371 --> 00:56:16.289
What do you mean?

669
00:56:17.499 --> 00:56:18.541
Why me?

670
00:56:18.625 --> 00:56:20.543
Because you got
the biggest mouth.

671
00:56:20.627 --> 00:56:22.628
That's for damn sure.

672
00:56:24.131 --> 00:56:25.131
(ELEVATOR DINGS)

673
00:56:25.507 --> 00:56:26.507
(HUMMING)

674
00:56:29.344 --> 00:56:30.344
Ooh.

675
00:56:32.139 --> 00:56:33.723
Hello, beautiful.

676
00:56:33.807 --> 00:56:36.434
Look at those dimples.
Sexy, sexy.

677
00:56:36.518 --> 00:56:38.561
Love those glasses.
Where did you get them from?

678
00:56:38.645 --> 00:56:41.064
Are those like Gucci frames
or something?

679
00:56:41.148 --> 00:56:42.315
No English?

680
00:56:42.399 --> 00:56:45.193
No, no, no. Damn.

681
00:56:45.736 --> 00:56:46.819
How are you, sir?

682
00:56:47.237 --> 00:56:51.074
Special Agent O'Conner.
US Federal Bureau
of Investigation.

683
00:56:51.158 --> 00:56:52.366
It says Caucasian.

684
00:56:52.659 --> 00:56:55.411
That's a tan.
You know, a tan?

685
00:56:58.332 --> 00:57:02.376
Look, I'm working
this case and I got some
evidence here to be held.

686
00:57:02.461 --> 00:57:04.837
But I need to get in
and check your
storage facility first.

687
00:57:04.922 --> 00:57:05.922
Nope.

688
00:57:06.006 --> 00:57:09.300
Look, I know you're
a true professional,
and I respect you, I promise.

689
00:57:09.384 --> 00:57:11.552
You know, it looks like
you work out
a little bit, too.

690
00:57:11.637 --> 00:57:14.097
What do you bench,
about 350?

691
00:57:14.515 --> 00:57:15.515
Ah, shit.

692
00:57:16.683 --> 00:57:18.017
Look, I'm just trying
to do my job, man.

693
00:57:18.102 --> 00:57:20.978
My boss sent me here
to just make sure
that everything was safe.

694
00:57:21.063 --> 00:57:22.063
It will be safe.

695
00:57:22.147 --> 00:57:24.232
Let me just come in
and take a quick peek.

696
00:57:24.316 --> 00:57:25.316
Nope.

697
00:57:25.400 --> 00:57:27.944
Come on, man.
Hook a brother up,
please?

698
00:57:28.028 --> 00:57:29.654
Nope. And you're
not my brother.

699
00:57:29.738 --> 00:57:30.988
Brother from
another mother?

700
00:57:31.073 --> 00:57:34.283
Look! No one enters
the facility but authorized
evidence personnel.

701
00:57:34.368 --> 00:57:35.576
Now stop wasting my time.

702
00:57:35.661 --> 00:57:36.619
I'm going to call
the embassy.

703
00:57:36.703 --> 00:57:38.162
No, no, no!
No, we're good.

704
00:57:38.497 --> 00:57:40.623
We don't need to call them.
For what? We're good.

705
00:57:40.707 --> 00:57:43.292
Here, I got the box.
We're all good.

706
00:57:43.377 --> 00:57:46.295
I promise you.
Thank you so much
for your time.

707
00:57:46.380 --> 00:57:48.589
Swear to God, if you
were on the other
side of that glass

708
00:57:48.674 --> 00:57:51.050
I'd bust your damn face in.
Now translate that.

709
00:58:08.902 --> 00:58:12.613
It's done. See, I think
I make a better special
agent than you ever did.

710
00:58:12.698 --> 00:58:13.698
(LAUGHING)

711
00:58:14.366 --> 00:58:16.659
Well, that depends
on how you define "special."

712
00:58:19.705 --> 00:58:20.997
TEJ: Come on, now.
Let's see what we got.

713
00:58:21.081 --> 00:58:22.582
Not funny.

714
00:58:24.334 --> 00:58:25.334
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

715
00:58:29.923 --> 00:58:31.632
All right, come on.

716
00:58:36.680 --> 00:58:38.181
Dawg,
you still can't drive.

717
00:58:39.808 --> 00:58:42.810
Now, I see why
you're always
getting into accidents.

718
00:58:42.895 --> 00:58:45.104
You can't even drive
a damn remote control car.

719
00:58:45.189 --> 00:58:47.106
I'm going to need you
to shut up right now.

720
00:58:47.191 --> 00:58:49.317
I'm not going to shut up.
Shut up.

721
00:58:49.401 --> 00:58:50.776
Strap him in his
safety belt, man.

722
00:58:53.989 --> 00:58:55.531
Give me the remote,
dawg. Go left.

723
00:58:55.616 --> 00:58:57.742
It looks like something
right over there
to the left. What is that?

724
00:58:57.826 --> 00:58:58.826
BRIAN: What is that?

725
00:59:00.204 --> 00:59:01.204
Bingo.

726
00:59:02.456 --> 00:59:04.457
What is that,
six-by-six?

727
00:59:04.541 --> 00:59:05.625
Eight-by-twelve.

728
00:59:05.709 --> 00:59:07.210
Seven-by-twelve.

729
00:59:07.294 --> 00:59:10.421
Fitted with 18-inch-thick
steel reinforced walls

730
00:59:10.505 --> 00:59:14.050
with a insulated copper
core to protect
against thermal lance.

731
00:59:14.134 --> 00:59:17.595
A Class-3 electronic
lock with a surefire
Griffin retumbler

732
00:59:17.679 --> 00:59:19.388
and a biometric palm scanner.

733
00:59:19.473 --> 00:59:21.974
Ten tons of
top-of-the-line security.

734
00:59:22.059 --> 00:59:23.726
Do I want to know
how you know all that?

735
00:59:23.810 --> 00:59:25.811
I had a life before
you knew me, O'Conner.

736
00:59:25.896 --> 00:59:27.730
Let's just leave it
at that, all right?

737
00:59:27.814 --> 00:59:29.482
She is a beauty,
though, man.

738
00:59:29.566 --> 00:59:31.734
A "beauty"
as in "good"?

739
00:59:31.818 --> 00:59:34.570
"Beauty" as in, she's
going to start off
playing hard to get.

740
00:59:34.655 --> 00:59:38.908
Then, no matter how much
I caress her, no matter
how much I love her,

741
00:59:38.992 --> 00:59:42.245
in the end,
she still ain't going
to give up that ass.

742
00:59:42.621 --> 00:59:43.621
(ALL LAUGHING)

743
00:59:47.709 --> 00:59:48.751
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

744
00:59:48.835 --> 00:59:50.336
Two to one says
you blow the wrong pipe.

745
00:59:50.712 --> 00:59:52.755
Yo, why you got to be
so negative all the time, man?

746
00:59:52.839 --> 00:59:53.881
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

747
00:59:53.966 --> 00:59:55.299
I ain't negative.

748
00:59:55.384 --> 00:59:58.177
I'm just positive
you're going to mess it up.

749
00:59:58.553 --> 01:00:01.555
I'm telling you, man,
you got issues.

750
01:00:06.353 --> 01:00:10.022
Next time if
there's no elevator,
I'm not coming.

751
01:00:10.565 --> 01:00:13.567
You need to learn
to relax, loco.

752
01:00:30.210 --> 01:00:31.210
(TIMER BEEPING)

753
01:00:34.089 --> 01:00:35.131
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

754
01:00:35.215 --> 01:00:37.258
You better hurry up,
we got less than a minute.

755
01:00:37.342 --> 01:00:43.306
Why do you always set
the timer so short?

756
01:00:59.573 --> 01:01:00.573
(SCREAMING)

757
01:01:05.454 --> 01:01:06.662
(RICO SPEAKING SPANISH)

758
01:01:06.747 --> 01:01:07.997
I hope you know
where you're going.

759
01:01:08.081 --> 01:01:10.916
I got this. Relax, man.

760
01:01:11.084 --> 01:01:12.918
Relax.

761
01:01:17.215 --> 01:01:18.215
(WHIMPERS)

762
01:01:24.056 --> 01:01:25.056
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

763
01:01:25.140 --> 01:01:26.766
...a police station.

764
01:01:27.142 --> 01:01:28.559
Relax.

765
01:01:37.611 --> 01:01:38.611
(EXCLAIMS)

766
01:01:39.237 --> 01:01:40.279
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

767
01:01:40.364 --> 01:01:42.198
You used too much
explosive! Again.

768
01:01:43.283 --> 01:01:44.950
Too much, too little...

769
01:01:45.535 --> 01:01:46.535
It's all the same.

770
01:01:47.204 --> 01:01:52.041
That's some Buddha shit
you learned from a book in
the prison library, isn't it?

771
01:01:53.210 --> 01:01:54.752
And what you're doing
there on the wall...

772
01:01:54.836 --> 01:01:57.630
You got that from
the same book, huh?

773
01:01:58.131 --> 01:01:59.131
You're so negative, bro.

774
01:02:25.992 --> 01:02:28.327
Can I have some light?

775
01:02:31.748 --> 01:02:34.125
MIA: Got it. We got it!

776
01:02:34.209 --> 01:02:35.835
BRIAN: Yeah, we're looking
at four cameras.

777
01:02:36.169 --> 01:02:38.379
Yo, that's some
high-end shit, too.

778
01:02:38.463 --> 01:02:39.505
Marker optics.

779
01:02:40.048 --> 01:02:41.882
Hundred-degree
field-of-view.

780
01:02:42.175 --> 01:02:43.676
Ten seconds oscillation.

781
01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:45.761
Yeah, that's
a narrow window, man.

782
01:02:45.846 --> 01:02:47.513
Can't we just tap in
and replace the image?

783
01:02:47.597 --> 01:02:49.598
No, it's hooked
into a digital sync.

784
01:02:49.683 --> 01:02:51.684
They would know we were
in the system.

785
01:02:51.768 --> 01:02:53.811
The best we can do is peek.

786
01:02:53.895 --> 01:02:56.480
We're going to need
some real fast cars
to get through this.

787
01:02:56.565 --> 01:02:58.023
Not just fast.

788
01:02:58.316 --> 01:03:00.526
You got a hard right
and a hairpin.

789
01:03:00.610 --> 01:03:02.278
We're going to need
something agile.

790
01:03:02.362 --> 01:03:04.113
You guys mock up a track.

791
01:03:04.197 --> 01:03:05.197
O'Conner.

792
01:03:06.533 --> 01:03:07.950
Let's go get some cars.

793
01:03:08.410 --> 01:03:09.869
Nice.

794
01:03:48.742 --> 01:03:51.076
Home sweet home.
(LAUGHING)

795
01:04:09.012 --> 01:04:10.137
BRIAN: Or that.

796
01:04:11.014 --> 01:04:13.516
How about that?
All motor, no tuning issues.

797
01:04:13.600 --> 01:04:15.935
I always wanted one of those.

798
01:04:16.019 --> 01:04:19.605
Held the record
on the Avenida
three years running.

799
01:04:19.856 --> 01:04:20.940
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

800
01:04:21.024 --> 01:04:22.107
Damn, bro...

801
01:04:22.192 --> 01:04:24.818
You got a lot of balls
to bring your problems
here, Toretto.

802
01:04:25.195 --> 01:04:28.072
Not to mention a cop.

803
01:04:28.156 --> 01:04:30.366
Yeah, we can keep
that on the low.

804
01:04:30.450 --> 01:04:33.410
Word on the street is
a lot of people are
looking for you two.

805
01:04:34.371 --> 01:04:35.371
What?

806
01:04:35.705 --> 01:04:37.414
You didn't think
we'd recognize you?

807
01:04:38.792 --> 01:04:40.793
No, we're kind
of counting on it.

808
01:04:41.211 --> 01:04:43.546
That little coupe
may run the streets
around here,

809
01:04:45.048 --> 01:04:49.093
but that monster
has never seen
a set of tail lights.

810
01:04:49.803 --> 01:04:51.136
Ever.
Well, she's about to.

811
01:04:52.138 --> 01:04:53.138
(DIOGO SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

812
01:04:53.223 --> 01:04:54.348
Dominic Toretto's
ride in my garage.

813
01:04:55.433 --> 01:04:59.603
Now that...
will be a nice trophy.

814
01:05:01.356 --> 01:05:03.941
Let's go, legend.

815
01:05:04.859 --> 01:05:07.403
Car for car.

816
01:05:07.571 --> 01:05:09.321
Car for car?

817
01:05:09.698 --> 01:05:11.198
DIOGO: You want it,
come and get it.

818
01:05:12.993 --> 01:05:13.993
(ENGINE REVVING)

819
01:05:15.912 --> 01:05:17.746
Let's see what they got.

820
01:05:22.836 --> 01:05:23.836
(ROME LAUGHING)

821
01:05:24.170 --> 01:05:25.379
Really?

822
01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:30.259
Where did you get
that from? Papa Smurf?

823
01:05:30.343 --> 01:05:33.262
Okay, O'Conner,
give it your best shot.

824
01:05:56.328 --> 01:05:57.328
How was that one?

825
01:05:57.412 --> 01:05:58.412
Camera caught you.

826
01:05:59.080 --> 01:06:00.956
What?
Yeah, it still caught you.

827
01:06:01.041 --> 01:06:03.000
Man, I was milking
the hell out of
that thing, too.

828
01:06:03.710 --> 01:06:05.502
We're going to need
a faster car.

829
01:06:06.546 --> 01:06:07.546
(SHOUTING INCOMPREHENSIBLY)

830
01:06:10.091 --> 01:06:11.842
I want my money.
Come on, man.

831
01:06:15.555 --> 01:06:16.555
Yeah!

832
01:06:19.184 --> 01:06:21.060
Let's get it! Watch this.

833
01:06:27.734 --> 01:06:31.278
That's exactly why your ass
ain't been driving.

834
01:06:42.832 --> 01:06:44.500
I think I'm in love.

835
01:06:48.296 --> 01:06:49.797
That was real solid work.

836
01:06:49.881 --> 01:06:53.342
I think Camera 3
still caught you, though.

837
01:06:53.426 --> 01:06:54.635
Let's do it again.

838
01:07:02.143 --> 01:07:04.103
TEGO: That's the piggy bank
you ordered.

839
01:07:04.187 --> 01:07:06.105
You're kidding me.
Yep.

840
01:07:07.982 --> 01:07:10.776
Where in the hell
did y'all get one of these?

841
01:07:11.486 --> 01:07:13.278
Well, we had a life
before you met us.

842
01:07:14.614 --> 01:07:17.950
All right, I'll get to work
on the electronic tumbler

843
01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:20.202
but there's still
another problem.

844
01:07:20.870 --> 01:07:22.204
Palm scanner.

845
01:07:22.288 --> 01:07:24.081
And without Reyes' handprint,

846
01:07:24.416 --> 01:07:26.542
Houdini himself
couldn't open this bitch.

847
01:07:26.626 --> 01:07:28.627
How do you know
it's Reyes' handprint?

848
01:07:28.712 --> 01:07:30.462
You got $100 million
in a safe.

849
01:07:30.547 --> 01:07:32.256
You going to put
somebody else's
handprint on it?

850
01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:35.342
(TALKING SPANISH)
Now there you go
with that negativity, man.

851
01:07:35.427 --> 01:07:36.760
That shit is eating
you alive.

852
01:07:36.845 --> 01:07:38.095
You check that.

853
01:07:38.179 --> 01:07:40.222
Yo, check that.
Shut up!

854
01:07:40.306 --> 01:07:42.391
How are we supposed to get
Reyes' handprint?

855
01:07:43.685 --> 01:07:45.227
DOM: Han.

856
01:07:45.311 --> 01:07:46.311
You're up.

857
01:07:48.314 --> 01:07:51.150
Sure. Nothing like
the easy stuff.

858
01:07:51.985 --> 01:07:53.736
Let's go. I'll drive.

859
01:08:12.172 --> 01:08:14.173
I make six bodyguards.
Seven.

860
01:08:15.008 --> 01:08:18.135
You think that guy
with a fanny pack
is a tourist?

861
01:08:23.183 --> 01:08:25.642
So, how long were
you in the army?

862
01:08:25.727 --> 01:08:28.520
That gun you pulled
the other day was
a Jericho 941.

863
01:08:29.856 --> 01:08:31.607
Thumb-racking the slide?

864
01:08:31.691 --> 01:08:33.525
That was
straight-up Mossad.

865
01:08:34.611 --> 01:08:36.653
I got out of the military

866
01:08:37.864 --> 01:08:40.824
probably the same time
you quit smoking.

867
01:08:40.909 --> 01:08:42.868
The amount
of chips you eat,

868
01:08:43.328 --> 01:08:46.413
the way you always
have to keep your hands
and mouth busy,

869
01:08:46.498 --> 01:08:49.082
you were a
two-pack-a-day man
for sure.

870
01:08:51.169 --> 01:08:52.795
Unfiltered.

871
01:08:56.466 --> 01:08:57.883
Well, this is a bust.

872
01:08:59.052 --> 01:09:02.429
We're not going to be
able to get his
fingerprints out here.

873
01:09:02.514 --> 01:09:05.557
We need to do some
more recon, call in
a couple of extra guys.

874
01:09:05.642 --> 01:09:06.892
Or

875
01:09:07.310 --> 01:09:09.520
you don't send a man
to do a woman's job.

876
01:10:07.787 --> 01:10:10.539
We're going to figure
this out, I promise you.

877
01:10:13.835 --> 01:10:15.127
What's up?

878
01:10:15.753 --> 01:10:18.297
I thought you were
more of a thong man.

879
01:10:18.381 --> 01:10:19.715
We got the print.

880
01:10:21.301 --> 01:10:22.593
Where?

881
01:10:24.596 --> 01:10:26.555
Okay, that's crazy.

882
01:10:28.266 --> 01:10:32.769
So, did he just slap
that ass or did he grab
and hold on to it?

883
01:10:33.062 --> 01:10:34.062
(BOTH LAUGHING)

884
01:10:35.315 --> 01:10:37.399
Hey, this will work.

885
01:10:38.026 --> 01:10:39.276
TEJ: I'm impressed.

886
01:10:39.360 --> 01:10:41.361
Got it?
TEJ: Got it.

887
01:10:41.446 --> 01:10:43.155
But you still didn't
answer the question.

888
01:10:49.162 --> 01:10:51.580
Oh, no. Guys, guys!
Guys, we have a problem.

889
01:10:51.664 --> 01:10:53.916
The whole team just got burnt.

890
01:10:55.335 --> 01:10:57.169
Now we're all wanted.

891
01:10:59.339 --> 01:11:00.339
GISELE: How did this happen?

892
01:11:00.506 --> 01:11:04.092
US Diplomatic Security Service
issued the warrants.

893
01:11:04.177 --> 01:11:06.011
Agent L. Hobbs.

894
01:11:06.387 --> 01:11:07.387
Hold on one second.

895
01:11:08.514 --> 01:11:09.556
Hey, Dom.

896
01:11:11.225 --> 01:11:13.018
Is that the guy you saw
in the favela?

897
01:11:15.855 --> 01:11:16.980
Yeah.

898
01:11:17.357 --> 01:11:20.817
Hobbs is the leader
of the elite task force
for the DSS.

899
01:11:20.902 --> 01:11:22.027
So he's good.

900
01:11:22.111 --> 01:11:25.197
When the FBI wants
to find somebody,
that's who they call.

901
01:11:25.281 --> 01:11:27.032
Because he never
misses his mark.

902
01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:29.993
This guy is Old Testament.

903
01:11:30.370 --> 01:11:33.372
Blood, bullets, wrath of God.
That's his style.

904
01:11:33.748 --> 01:11:36.166
And right now
he's hunting us?

905
01:11:36.250 --> 01:11:37.960
Dom, we got to move up
our timeline.

906
01:11:38.044 --> 01:11:39.169
ROME: Yeah, but how?

907
01:11:39.253 --> 01:11:42.714
This thing's already been
difficult without Wyatt Earp
on our asses.

908
01:11:43.299 --> 01:11:45.050
If anything,
we need more room
to breathe.

909
01:11:47.387 --> 01:11:48.762
Roman's right.

910
01:11:51.599 --> 01:11:54.059
Think we need to get
some fresh air.

911
01:11:57.981 --> 01:12:00.065
We've got a hit.
'70s Charger.

912
01:12:00.149 --> 01:12:02.150
Let's get a move on!

913
01:12:05.571 --> 01:12:08.156
Eastbound on
Avenida Atlantica.

914
01:12:08.241 --> 01:12:09.658
Move, move, move, move!

915
01:12:15.915 --> 01:12:17.582
It stopped about
a block ahead.

916
01:12:18.251 --> 01:12:19.668
Park it.
We're going on foot.

917
01:12:42.984 --> 01:12:44.109
Hey, Toretto.

918
01:12:52.201 --> 01:12:53.827
You're under arrest.

919
01:12:54.120 --> 01:12:55.287
Arrest?

920
01:12:56.456 --> 01:12:58.373
I don't feel like
I'm under arrest.

921
01:12:59.125 --> 01:13:00.375
How about you,
Brian?

922
01:13:00.460 --> 01:13:01.626
No, not a bit.

923
01:13:03.588 --> 01:13:04.838
Not even a little bit.

924
01:13:04.922 --> 01:13:07.174
Just give it a minute.
It'll sink in.

925
01:13:10.595 --> 01:13:13.055
BRIAN: We didn't kill
those feds. That was Reyes.

926
01:13:13.139 --> 01:13:14.431
HOBBS: I don't give a shit.

927
01:13:14.515 --> 01:13:17.309
I'm just here to bring
in two assholes whose names
hit my desk.

928
01:13:17.602 --> 01:13:20.812
Yeah, that sounds
like a real hero.

929
01:13:23.858 --> 01:13:25.400
That's funny.

930
01:13:25.485 --> 01:13:28.570
From a guy who took the oath
of a cop, then went against
everything it stood for.

931
01:13:28.654 --> 01:13:30.405
Or some wannabe
tough guy prick

932
01:13:30.490 --> 01:13:32.866
who beat a man half
to death with
a socket wrench.

933
01:13:33.618 --> 01:13:34.826
Yeah, real tough.

934
01:13:35.828 --> 01:13:38.997
You turn around
and put your hands
behind your back.

935
01:13:40.166 --> 01:13:41.583
I don't think so.

936
01:13:41.667 --> 01:13:44.294
Your mistake is
thinking you got
a goddamn choice, boy.

937
01:13:48.466 --> 01:13:50.050
And your mistake?

938
01:13:50.676 --> 01:13:52.177
Thinking you're in America.

939
01:13:55.348 --> 01:13:58.850
You're a long way from home.

940
01:14:01.354 --> 01:14:03.855
This is Brazil.

941
01:14:19.080 --> 01:14:21.331
Come on, boss.
Another day.

942
01:14:23.042 --> 01:14:25.502
Come on, H,
it's a lot of heat.

943
01:14:30.716 --> 01:14:33.051
I'll see you soon,
Toretto.

944
01:14:34.387 --> 01:14:36.972
I look forward to it, cop.

945
01:15:14.260 --> 01:15:15.260
Yep.

946
01:15:15.344 --> 01:15:16.720
Tracker's on.

947
01:15:18.097 --> 01:15:19.097
Got them.

948
01:16:25.331 --> 01:16:27.707
I don't understand.
Why come here?

949
01:16:28.209 --> 01:16:31.044
Why risk it all
for $20 worth of silver?

950
01:16:34.632 --> 01:16:35.882
Because it's worth it.

951
01:16:39.679 --> 01:16:41.221
You should run,
you know.

952
01:16:41.973 --> 01:16:43.390
Hobbs will find you.

953
01:16:46.102 --> 01:16:49.020
You have every reason
to leave. Why stay?

954
01:16:56.445 --> 01:16:58.530
Why do you?

955
01:17:00.074 --> 01:17:02.075
My husband was
a good police officer.

956
01:17:02.910 --> 01:17:04.536
An honest man.

957
01:17:05.955 --> 01:17:07.664
We both grew up here.

958
01:17:08.708 --> 01:17:10.959
Two years ago he was
murdered in the street

959
01:17:11.043 --> 01:17:12.794
right outside our door.

960
01:17:15.298 --> 01:17:19.050
Reyes owns this favela now.
He gives things to people.

961
01:17:21.387 --> 01:17:23.680
But everything
has a price.

962
01:17:26.392 --> 01:17:28.143
The people here
need a new start.

963
01:17:28.728 --> 01:17:30.228
They need
to be free.

964
01:17:38.404 --> 01:17:39.404
(SIGHS)

965
01:17:40.114 --> 01:17:41.740
You didn't kill
those men in the train,

966
01:17:42.408 --> 01:17:43.700
did you?

967
01:17:48.247 --> 01:17:51.041
Now, why would you
believe anything
I would tell you?

968
01:17:57.923 --> 01:17:59.215
Hey!

969
01:18:02.595 --> 01:18:04.304
Was she so special to you?

970
01:18:09.101 --> 01:18:11.436
I never thought anyone
could understand how much.

971
01:18:14.899 --> 01:18:16.274
But you do.

972
01:18:39.465 --> 01:18:40.465
Yeah!

973
01:18:51.685 --> 01:18:52.977
Close, but not enough.

974
01:18:53.521 --> 01:18:55.105
Dom, the window
is too small, man.

975
01:18:55.189 --> 01:18:58.942
Only way we're going to
beat the cameras is
with invisible cars.

976
01:19:01.654 --> 01:19:04.030
And I know just where
to get them.

977
01:19:07.159 --> 01:19:08.451
Let's take a ride, boys.

978
01:19:16.335 --> 01:19:18.378
Don't hurt yourself.

979
01:19:37.022 --> 01:19:39.399
It's been a while since
I've been behind the wheel
of one of these.

980
01:19:39.692 --> 01:19:41.609
First time I've ever
been in the front seat.

981
01:19:42.236 --> 01:19:43.236
(CHUCKLES)

982
01:19:49.368 --> 01:19:50.910
Rome, what took
you so long?

983
01:19:51.287 --> 01:19:55.123
I thought for sure you'd be
showing up with some
chrome spinners or something.

984
01:19:56.208 --> 01:19:57.208
Real funny.

985
01:19:58.711 --> 01:20:02.338
I got $100,000 that says
I can take you all
in the next quarter-mile.

986
01:20:02.423 --> 01:20:03.965
Yeah, your broke ass
has got a hundred grand.

987
01:20:04.049 --> 01:20:06.384
If we pull off this job,
I will.

988
01:20:06.760 --> 01:20:08.219
The next two lights.

989
01:20:08.512 --> 01:20:09.679
Hundred thousand.

990
01:20:10.639 --> 01:20:13.433
We don't pull this job off,
we're probably dead anyway.

991
01:20:13.976 --> 01:20:16.019
Let's make it a million.

992
01:20:16.896 --> 01:20:19.230
I like that.
All right,
a million-dollar quarter-mile.

993
01:20:20.483 --> 01:20:22.025
All right, then.

994
01:20:22.318 --> 01:20:24.861
You only live once.
Let's do it.

995
01:20:25.362 --> 01:20:26.404
What do you say, Dom?

996
01:20:27.072 --> 01:20:28.531
We talking or we racing?

997
01:20:29.992 --> 01:20:31.075
Just don't cheat this time.

998
01:20:31.702 --> 01:20:34.329
Got to let that go.

999
01:20:34.580 --> 01:20:35.580
(ENGINES REVVING)

1000
01:20:52.932 --> 01:20:54.390
Yeah!

1001
01:20:57.478 --> 01:20:58.561
Typical, Roman.

1002
01:20:58.646 --> 01:21:01.105
I'm going to get
this money. I'm hungry.

1003
01:21:09.406 --> 01:21:11.074
Don't make it too
easy for me, boys.

1004
01:21:13.911 --> 01:21:14.911
No!

1005
01:21:16.121 --> 01:21:17.872
Not this time, Dom.

1006
01:21:22.711 --> 01:21:24.462
You got to want it, Brian.

1007
01:21:52.658 --> 01:21:56.494
Yeah! Owned you! Owned you!

1008
01:22:11.260 --> 01:22:13.553
Good race, O'Conner.
Thanks, Dom.

1009
01:22:15.514 --> 01:22:18.308
Do you know how long
I've been waiting
for that shit?

1010
01:22:18.392 --> 01:22:20.351
I told you
he didn't see it.

1011
01:22:20.561 --> 01:22:22.270
Your man right there?

1012
01:22:22.354 --> 01:22:24.772
He let off the throttle
at the line.

1013
01:22:24.857 --> 01:22:27.567
You didn't do nothing.
He let you win.

1014
01:22:28.527 --> 01:22:30.236
Bullshit.
(SCOFFING)

1015
01:22:51.383 --> 01:22:54.177
Vince, what are you doing?
Quiet! They've been
tracking you.

1016
01:23:01.685 --> 01:23:02.727
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

1017
01:23:02.811 --> 01:23:03.895
I know she's here!

1018
01:23:06.398 --> 01:23:07.565
Find her!

1019
01:23:07.733 --> 01:23:09.275
Go! Go! Go!

1020
01:23:23.666 --> 01:23:25.333
It's okay. Wait!

1021
01:23:25.417 --> 01:23:28.461
Reyes' guys were waiting
for me at the market.

1022
01:23:29.421 --> 01:23:31.047
Vince saved my life.

1023
01:23:36.470 --> 01:23:37.929
DOM: You hungry?

1024
01:23:41.100 --> 01:23:43.518
Yeah, sure.
Good.

1025
01:23:45.270 --> 01:23:46.479
Because you're saying grace.

1026
01:23:49.692 --> 01:23:51.109
Thanks, Vince.

1027
01:23:57.032 --> 01:23:58.157
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1028
01:23:58.242 --> 01:23:59.325
Yo, you burned it!

1029
01:23:59.410 --> 01:24:02.370
Yo, this is how my momma
does it. Relax.

1030
01:24:02.454 --> 01:24:04.789
Yeah, but your mom is the
worst cook in the world.

1031
01:24:04.915 --> 01:24:07.750
Yo, don't you be talking
about my momma.

1032
01:24:09.920 --> 01:24:12.422
Yeah, come on, baby.
Who's good living?

1033
01:24:12.506 --> 01:24:14.632
To you, bro.
Cheers, cheers, cheers.

1034
01:24:14.717 --> 01:24:16.968
ROME: So, we in Brazil.
It's the good life.

1035
01:24:17.052 --> 01:24:18.052
Yeah.

1036
01:24:18.137 --> 01:24:21.931
So, you got a little more
than $10 or $11 million
coming.

1037
01:24:22.015 --> 01:24:23.141
What you going to do
with your money?

1038
01:24:23.225 --> 01:24:24.892
Me?
Yeah.

1039
01:24:24.977 --> 01:24:27.729
Actually, man, I been
thinking about opening up
a garage back home.

1040
01:24:28.689 --> 01:24:31.482
Place where people can
bring their cars and not get
completely ripped off.

1041
01:24:31.567 --> 01:24:32.692
You know what I mean?

1042
01:24:32.776 --> 01:24:34.110
Really?
Yeah.

1043
01:24:34.194 --> 01:24:37.071
So, your dream is
to start a day job?

1044
01:24:37.156 --> 01:24:39.323
That's stupid.
Like, why would...

1045
01:24:39.408 --> 01:24:41.993
No, it's not stupid at all.
I love what I do.

1046
01:24:42.077 --> 01:24:43.077
That don't make
no sense to me.

1047
01:24:43.162 --> 01:24:45.997
I know what I'm going
to do with my money.

1048
01:24:48.000 --> 01:24:49.917
Buying some cooking lessons
for my man.

1049
01:24:50.419 --> 01:24:51.878
See? See?

1050
01:24:51.962 --> 01:24:54.255
There you go with
that negativity, man.

1051
01:24:54.339 --> 01:24:56.382
You know me.
Money ain't a goddamn thing.

1052
01:24:56.467 --> 01:24:59.010
It's going to take
a little more than money
to learn how to cook.

1053
01:24:59.094 --> 01:25:00.344
That's horrible.

1054
01:25:00.888 --> 01:25:04.557
But I heard they was looking
for a chef down at
this animal shelter.

1055
01:25:04.641 --> 01:25:05.725
You might want to...

1056
01:25:05.809 --> 01:25:07.518
I know the manager.

1057
01:25:12.941 --> 01:25:14.609
Hey, Dom.

1058
01:25:17.321 --> 01:25:18.821
Listen.

1059
01:25:19.573 --> 01:25:23.284
I know that you're all set
for this job tomorrow,

1060
01:25:23.368 --> 01:25:25.119
but if you need
an extra man, I could...

1061
01:25:25.204 --> 01:25:26.537
You're in.

1062
01:25:34.963 --> 01:25:36.506
There's always
room for family.

1063
01:25:42.971 --> 01:25:44.013
Thank you.

1064
01:25:48.602 --> 01:25:49.727
Get something to eat.

1065
01:25:51.522 --> 01:25:53.147
Yeah.

1066
01:25:55.025 --> 01:25:56.734
Can you believe
Mia calls this a curse?

1067
01:26:00.531 --> 01:26:02.698
She might be right.

1068
01:26:07.037 --> 01:26:09.497
You really like doing
that stuff, huh?

1069
01:26:09.748 --> 01:26:14.001
When your life is on
the line that's when you
learn about yourself.

1070
01:26:18.966 --> 01:26:20.716
That's a fair deal.

1071
01:26:24.012 --> 01:26:28.140
We're less than 24 hours
from the biggest celebration
of our life.

1072
01:26:28.225 --> 01:26:30.518
Y'all need a refill.
This is serious stuff.

1073
01:26:30.602 --> 01:26:31.894
No, I'm good.
Cheers, baby.

1074
01:26:31.979 --> 01:26:33.604
I'm good.
No, thank you.

1075
01:26:33.689 --> 01:26:34.689
No, she can't.

1076
01:26:36.942 --> 01:26:38.943
What do you mean?
She can't.

1077
01:26:39.278 --> 01:26:41.946
What do you mean
she can't? What is...

1078
01:26:46.118 --> 01:26:48.369
Are you serious right now?
(LAUGHING)

1079
01:26:48.453 --> 01:26:52.164
Is that the reason you let him
beat you in the quarter-mile?

1080
01:26:53.500 --> 01:26:56.752
That was a baby gift.
No, that's messed up.

1081
01:26:56.837 --> 01:26:58.421
No, you're not taking
that from me.

1082
01:26:58.505 --> 01:27:00.131
Wait, wait,
hold on a second.

1083
01:27:00.215 --> 01:27:04.510
So, did he just smack
the ass or did he grab
and hold on to it?

1084
01:27:04.887 --> 01:27:05.887
Which one was it?

1085
01:27:05.971 --> 01:27:08.472
Congratulations.
Thank you.

1086
01:27:08.599 --> 01:27:10.391
ROME: How can you keep
this a secret?

1087
01:27:10.475 --> 01:27:12.476
Crazy, huh?
ROME: It's your boy.

1088
01:27:12.603 --> 01:27:16.147
ROME: Why would you keep
something like that
away from me?

1089
01:27:16.481 --> 01:27:18.274
Baby gift, huh?

1090
01:27:18.525 --> 01:27:21.360
I have no idea
what they're talking about.
Oh?

1091
01:27:21.445 --> 01:27:24.447
TEJ: What happened
to the pull-out method, man?

1092
01:27:25.532 --> 01:27:27.575
Toast.
Toast.

1093
01:27:35.918 --> 01:27:39.170
Money will come and go.
We know that.

1094
01:27:40.297 --> 01:27:43.674
But the most important
thing in life will always
be the people in this room.

1095
01:27:45.093 --> 01:27:46.344
Right here.

1096
01:27:48.972 --> 01:27:50.014
Right now.

1097
01:27:53.143 --> 01:27:54.143
(SPEAKING ITALIAN)

1098
01:27:55.187 --> 01:27:56.187
(ALL REPLYING IN ITALIAN)

1099
01:28:04.613 --> 01:28:06.197
I'm all set.

1100
01:28:07.199 --> 01:28:10.201
HAN: Yo, Santos. Van good?

1101
01:28:11.286 --> 01:28:13.496
You know we're
always good, bro.

1102
01:28:17.376 --> 01:28:20.127
Hobbs is on the other side
of the city.

1103
01:28:20.212 --> 01:28:22.797
We're not going
to get a better window.

1104
01:28:22.881 --> 01:28:25.132
Okay, guys,
it's show time!

1105
01:28:25.217 --> 01:28:26.801
First team in position,
let's go.

1106
01:28:26.885 --> 01:28:28.135
TEGO: Come on, let's do this.

1107
01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:41.440
Hey, Dom.

1108
01:28:43.276 --> 01:28:44.402
I got eyes on Mia.

1109
01:28:49.408 --> 01:28:52.493
Moscow, Bali, Goa, Hong Kong.

1110
01:28:53.120 --> 01:28:54.996
And what do they all
have in common?

1111
01:28:55.080 --> 01:28:56.163
No extradition.

1112
01:28:58.250 --> 01:29:01.002
We're one hour away
from the rest of our lives.

1113
01:29:01.086 --> 01:29:02.378
Yeah.

1114
01:29:04.089 --> 01:29:05.089
Cops!

1115
01:29:07.676 --> 01:29:09.051
Come on. Go.

1116
01:29:20.647 --> 01:29:22.273
You just made a big mistake.

1117
01:29:23.775 --> 01:29:25.693
Took me a while to find
that tracking chip.

1118
01:29:26.194 --> 01:29:27.570
But not as long
to flip the receiver.

1119
01:29:27.654 --> 01:29:29.155
You're going down, Toretto.

1120
01:29:29.489 --> 01:29:31.282
I'm right here.

1121
01:29:31.491 --> 01:29:32.491
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1122
01:30:46.191 --> 01:30:47.191
(YELLING)

1123
01:30:59.412 --> 01:31:01.413
Dom!
Stand back. I got this.

1124
01:31:07.337 --> 01:31:11.257
Pull off!
Dom! Please, stop!

1125
01:31:16.888 --> 01:31:17.888
Dom!

1126
01:31:27.065 --> 01:31:28.399
Dom!
(DOM SCREAMING)

1127
01:32:28.960 --> 01:32:29.960
(WALKIE TALKIE BEEPING)

1128
01:32:30.921 --> 01:32:31.962
Yeah.

1129
01:32:33.340 --> 01:32:35.299
We're coming in now.

1130
01:32:36.885 --> 01:32:39.553
Have the marshals meet us
at the airport when we land.

1131
01:32:47.437 --> 01:32:48.812
Ambush!

1132
01:33:06.456 --> 01:33:09.667
Wilkes, suppression fire.
Shut them down.

1133
01:33:13.880 --> 01:33:15.547
Stagger-step. Cover me.

1134
01:33:20.553 --> 01:33:21.595
Watch them!

1135
01:33:33.191 --> 01:33:34.275
Cut us loose!

1136
01:33:34.359 --> 01:33:36.360
Come on! Cut us loose!

1137
01:35:34.813 --> 01:35:36.188
We're good?
Yeah, let's go, let's go!

1138
01:35:46.825 --> 01:35:47.825
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1139
01:35:58.294 --> 01:35:59.294
(SPITTING)

1140
01:36:09.472 --> 01:36:11.098
VINCE: Hey, Dom.

1141
01:36:17.355 --> 01:36:19.523
You've got to meet my son.

1142
01:36:19.816 --> 01:36:21.567
Nico.

1143
01:36:26.322 --> 01:36:27.781
I will.

1144
01:36:30.702 --> 01:36:31.952
He's a good kid.

1145
01:36:35.790 --> 01:36:38.417
You know,
we named him after you.

1146
01:36:40.211 --> 01:36:41.545
"Dominic."

1147
01:36:48.803 --> 01:36:50.804
You've got
my word, Vince.

1148
01:36:57.353 --> 01:36:59.438
You were
always my brother.

1149
01:37:09.073 --> 01:37:11.575
I got eyes on Nico now.

1150
01:37:22.253 --> 01:37:24.671
We need to move.
We don't have that much time.

1151
01:37:24.756 --> 01:37:25.881
I got us a flight out.

1152
01:37:25.965 --> 01:37:28.550
We can leave Rio
in the rearview
in the next five hours.

1153
01:37:28.635 --> 01:37:30.427
Not to run away.

1154
01:37:31.846 --> 01:37:33.430
To finish the job.

1155
01:37:34.265 --> 01:37:36.683
Are you crazy, Dom?
We can't.

1156
01:37:37.268 --> 01:37:38.852
ROME: It's a suicide mission.

1157
01:37:39.938 --> 01:37:41.605
That's your man
over there on the table.

1158
01:37:42.982 --> 01:37:45.025
The plan is busted!

1159
01:37:45.318 --> 01:37:47.819
This is bullshit, man.
Reyes knows we're coming!

1160
01:37:47.904 --> 01:37:49.279
TEJ: He's right.

1161
01:37:49.572 --> 01:37:52.366
They tripled the detail
at the police station.

1162
01:37:52.784 --> 01:37:55.035
TEJ: It's going to be
a wall of gunfire.

1163
01:37:57.247 --> 01:37:59.331
Reyes doesn't get
away with this.

1164
01:37:59.624 --> 01:38:00.624
It's a trap, man.

1165
01:38:00.708 --> 01:38:02.125
You know that.

1166
01:38:02.794 --> 01:38:05.128
Dom, listen to them.

1167
01:38:05.797 --> 01:38:08.382
Run, before it's
too late. Leave Rio.

1168
01:38:09.759 --> 01:38:11.093
You can be free.

1169
01:38:13.263 --> 01:38:15.264
Running ain't freedom.

1170
01:38:16.724 --> 01:38:18.141
You should know that.

1171
01:38:23.231 --> 01:38:25.649
You know you're all free
to make your own choices.

1172
01:38:29.862 --> 01:38:30.988
HOBBS: I'm in.

1173
01:38:40.373 --> 01:38:41.999
I'll ride with you,
Toretto.

1174
01:38:45.295 --> 01:38:47.838
At least until we kill
that son of a bitch.

1175
01:38:56.264 --> 01:38:57.848
BRIAN: So what's
the plan, Dom?

1176
01:38:58.683 --> 01:39:00.726
We can't just go
sneaking around anymore.

1177
01:39:02.228 --> 01:39:04.187
We don't sneak.

1178
01:39:04.981 --> 01:39:08.108
The only thing
he cares about
is his money.

1179
01:39:08.359 --> 01:39:09.693
We pull that,

1180
01:39:10.695 --> 01:39:12.112
we pull him.

1181
01:39:24.542 --> 01:39:25.584
(SECURITY DOOR BUZZING)

1182
01:39:28.379 --> 01:39:29.421
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

1183
01:39:29.505 --> 01:39:30.547
See?

1184
01:39:31.716 --> 01:39:34.384
I called in every cop
on our payroll.

1185
01:39:35.887 --> 01:39:37.679
We're covered.

1186
01:39:39.390 --> 01:39:40.807
We've got every
entrance covered
with weapons teams.

1187
01:39:40.892 --> 01:39:43.644
God Himself couldn't
get at your money
if He wanted to.

1188
01:39:44.145 --> 01:39:48.482
God isn't my worry.

1189
01:39:58.242 --> 01:39:59.242
You ready?

1190
01:40:01.537 --> 01:40:02.537
I'm ready.

1191
01:40:40.076 --> 01:40:41.076
(POLICE OFFICERS CHATTERING)

1192
01:40:59.679 --> 01:41:00.804
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

1193
01:41:00.888 --> 01:41:02.013
What's happening?

1194
01:41:02.098 --> 01:41:03.557
They're taking the vault!

1195
01:41:03.641 --> 01:41:05.308
What?
The vault!

1196
01:41:14.861 --> 01:41:18.113
Follow me! Quickly!

1197
01:41:22.452 --> 01:41:23.952
Let me through!

1198
01:41:34.005 --> 01:41:35.005
Don't move!

1199
01:41:36.215 --> 01:41:37.591
Stay down.

1200
01:42:07.580 --> 01:42:08.955
Call it out, Mia!

1201
01:42:09.040 --> 01:42:10.540
You've got a straight shot
for two blocks.

1202
01:42:12.043 --> 01:42:13.543
Go right.
Got it.

1203
01:42:21.302 --> 01:42:22.302
(PEDESTRIANS SCREAMING)

1204
01:42:35.942 --> 01:42:37.526
Well, the plan is working.

1205
01:42:37.610 --> 01:42:42.489
You guys have every
corrupt cop in Rio on your
tail. You have to move fast.

1206
01:42:42.573 --> 01:42:43.657
What's the best route?

1207
01:42:43.741 --> 01:42:46.993
Okay, keep going straight
another half-mile
onto Rua Fonseca,

1208
01:42:47.078 --> 01:42:48.995
and then go left.

1209
01:42:52.750 --> 01:42:53.792
That ain't going to work.

1210
01:42:55.878 --> 01:42:57.462
Spikes ahead, Dom.
We got spikes!

1211
01:42:57.880 --> 01:42:59.464
We're going right!

1212
01:43:00.842 --> 01:43:02.133
No, it's too tight,
we're not going to fit.

1213
01:43:02.218 --> 01:43:03.677
We've got no choice. Now!

1214
01:43:13.104 --> 01:43:14.104
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1215
01:43:23.364 --> 01:43:24.531
Shit!

1216
01:43:31.163 --> 01:43:32.455
Holy shit!

1217
01:43:32.540 --> 01:43:35.417
Guys, I am hearing
all this chatter. Did you
just take out a bank?

1218
01:43:44.468 --> 01:43:45.468
Two inbound!

1219
01:43:47.889 --> 01:43:49.347
All right, there's an alley
coming up on your left.

1220
01:43:49.432 --> 01:43:51.099
Yeah, I got it.

1221
01:44:30.640 --> 01:44:31.640
(GUNSHOTS)

1222
01:44:37.688 --> 01:44:38.688
(BRAKES SCREECHING)

1223
01:44:39.315 --> 01:44:40.315
(GRUNTING)

1224
01:44:44.487 --> 01:44:46.112
You little bastard!

1225
01:45:09.261 --> 01:45:11.972
All right, good job, Dom.
Right-hander, right here,
right-hander.

1226
01:45:18.354 --> 01:45:20.397
Guys, there's a big group
coming at you from the south.

1227
01:45:20.481 --> 01:45:22.273
You have to do something now!

1228
01:45:25.152 --> 01:45:26.194
Hey, go wide.

1229
01:45:48.175 --> 01:45:49.175
(WOMAN SCREAMING)

1230
01:45:49.885 --> 01:45:50.885
(CHUCKLING)

1231
01:45:58.978 --> 01:45:59.978
Yeah!

1232
01:46:18.748 --> 01:46:19.748
(POLICE CAR HONKING)

1233
01:46:38.184 --> 01:46:39.184
(BULLETS HITTING CAR)

1234
01:47:04.335 --> 01:47:05.335
(GRUNTING)

1235
01:47:13.844 --> 01:47:15.136
You're all clear on the left.

1236
01:47:15.221 --> 01:47:17.055
Good afternoon, officer!

1237
01:47:19.058 --> 01:47:21.476
License and registration,
please!

1238
01:47:27.691 --> 01:47:30.568
Yes! This is big-boy stuff!

1239
01:47:30.653 --> 01:47:32.070
We're clear on the right.

1240
01:47:32.321 --> 01:47:33.404
Oh, man.

1241
01:47:40.204 --> 01:47:41.246
Thanks, guys.

1242
01:47:41.622 --> 01:47:42.747
Any time.

1243
01:47:43.040 --> 01:47:44.624
I'll see you on
the other side.

1244
01:47:44.708 --> 01:47:47.001
You guys just carved out
a 10-second window.

1245
01:47:47.086 --> 01:47:48.545
Make it count!

1246
01:47:54.718 --> 01:47:55.802
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

1247
01:47:55.886 --> 01:47:57.053
Zizi, stay on them.

1248
01:48:23.581 --> 01:48:25.498
They can't outrun us
on the bridge.

1249
01:48:27.459 --> 01:48:28.459
Shit.

1250
01:48:35.551 --> 01:48:36.759
They have no way out.

1251
01:48:38.762 --> 01:48:39.762
No!

1252
01:48:40.598 --> 01:48:41.681
There's too many of them.

1253
01:48:41.765 --> 01:48:43.725
Hey, there's too many of them.
We're not going to make it.

1254
01:48:47.438 --> 01:48:48.438
You're right, we aren't.

1255
01:48:49.732 --> 01:48:50.690
You are.

1256
01:48:50.774 --> 01:48:52.066
What are you talking about?

1257
01:48:52.276 --> 01:48:54.694
Just let the vault go.
Get out of there.

1258
01:48:54.778 --> 01:48:56.487
You're a father now, Brian.

1259
01:48:56.572 --> 01:48:58.740
No, I'm not leaving you.
Now you stick with the plan!

1260
01:48:59.450 --> 01:49:00.825
It was always the plan.

1261
01:49:01.577 --> 01:49:02.869
Take care of Mia.

1262
01:49:02.953 --> 01:49:05.371
Dom, you listen
to me now. Okay?

1263
01:49:05.456 --> 01:49:07.290
You cut loose right now.

1264
01:49:23.599 --> 01:49:24.557
(SPEAKING PORTUGUESE)

1265
01:49:24.642 --> 01:49:25.683
Hey, what is he doing?

1266
01:49:29.647 --> 01:49:30.772
We've got him!

1267
01:49:47.623 --> 01:49:48.873
Close down the bridge!

1268
01:50:23.117 --> 01:50:24.492
Do something, asshole!

1269
01:50:36.588 --> 01:50:37.714
Kill him, dammit!

1270
01:50:49.101 --> 01:50:50.560
Kill him now!

1271
01:51:21.633 --> 01:51:22.633
(SCREAMING)

1272
01:51:47.701 --> 01:51:48.701
(PANTING)

1273
01:52:02.257 --> 01:52:04.967
I thought I told you
to go on.

1274
01:52:06.929 --> 01:52:09.138
Yeah, I had
to make a call.

1275
01:52:23.654 --> 01:52:24.654
(GROANING)

1276
01:52:26.740 --> 01:52:28.157
Help me.

1277
01:52:30.536 --> 01:52:32.537
That's for my team,
you son of a bitch.

1278
01:52:36.708 --> 01:52:38.418
It's a hell of a mess.

1279
01:52:39.128 --> 01:52:40.753
Yeah, it is.

1280
01:52:42.256 --> 01:52:44.006
You know I can't
let you two go.

1281
01:52:44.508 --> 01:52:46.092
I ain't made that way.

1282
01:52:48.846 --> 01:52:51.514
The way I see it,
you've earned
yourselves 24 hours.

1283
01:52:52.683 --> 01:52:53.683
The money stays, though.

1284
01:52:55.018 --> 01:52:57.186
If I were you,
I'd use the time.

1285
01:52:57.521 --> 01:53:00.523
Make peace with
whatever demons
you got left.

1286
01:53:04.987 --> 01:53:06.863
Because come tomorrow,

1287
01:53:08.240 --> 01:53:09.365
I will find you.

1288
01:53:21.211 --> 01:53:22.503
Toretto!

1289
01:53:23.422 --> 01:53:24.714
I'll see you soon.

1290
01:53:27.551 --> 01:53:29.427
No, you won't.

1291
01:54:10.886 --> 01:54:11.969
Thanks, guys.

1292
01:54:12.054 --> 01:54:13.554
I'll see you
on the other side.

1293
01:54:18.435 --> 01:54:20.895
You guys just carved out
a 10 second window.

1294
01:54:20.979 --> 01:54:22.271
Make it count!

1295
01:54:38.121 --> 01:54:39.121
(LAUGHING)

1296
01:54:53.554 --> 01:54:54.554
(COMPUTER BEEPING)

1297
01:55:04.690 --> 01:55:06.399
Come on, baby.

1298
01:55:06.483 --> 01:55:08.359
Don't be mean.

1299
01:55:10.612 --> 01:55:11.612
Come on.

1300
01:55:13.198 --> 01:55:14.198
(VAULT SCANNER BEEPING)

1301
01:55:17.160 --> 01:55:18.160
(VAULT UNLOCKING)
(SIGHING)

1302
01:55:49.651 --> 01:55:50.651
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1303
01:56:23.226 --> 01:56:26.687
"For Rosa and Nico.
See you soon,
- Uncle Dom"

1304
01:56:33.570 --> 01:56:37.031
MONACO

1305
01:56:38.575 --> 01:56:39.659
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

1306
01:56:39.743 --> 01:56:40.826
You sure about this?

1307
01:56:42.621 --> 01:56:44.080
You know I am.

1308
01:56:46.041 --> 01:56:47.500
You don't need to do this.

1309
01:56:48.502 --> 01:56:50.836
Just leave me alone.

1310
01:56:50.921 --> 01:56:52.963
Bro, I'm not trying
to be negative,
but casinos

1311
01:56:53.173 --> 01:56:55.883
are the kinds of places
designed to take money
from guys like you and me.

1312
01:56:56.051 --> 01:56:59.720
When I win here
I'm buying you a lifetime
supply of antidepressants.

1313
01:57:00.013 --> 01:57:03.015
You don't put
ten million on red!

1314
01:57:03.100 --> 01:57:04.058
Enough already.

1315
01:57:04.142 --> 01:57:05.518
You put it on black.

1316
01:57:07.062 --> 01:57:08.020
(SPEAKING FRENCH)

1317
01:57:08.105 --> 01:57:09.230
No more bets.

1318
01:57:35.257 --> 01:57:37.466
Right this way, my dear.

1319
01:57:39.511 --> 01:57:41.345
You stay right here,
I'll be right back.

1320
01:57:43.181 --> 01:57:45.349
So, this is
your dream, huh?

1321
01:57:45.434 --> 01:57:46.726
It's enough for me, man.

1322
01:57:46.810 --> 01:57:48.227
I take it that's
your dream.

1323
01:57:48.311 --> 01:57:50.896
Absolutely. What up, boy?
What's going on?

1324
01:57:50.981 --> 01:57:52.773
You good?
Yes, yes.

1325
01:57:52.858 --> 01:57:54.066
You know what's crazy?

1326
01:57:54.151 --> 01:57:56.736
There's only four
of those cars
in the whole world.

1327
01:57:57.279 --> 01:57:59.697
Yeah, I got the only one
in the Western Hemisphere.

1328
01:58:00.198 --> 01:58:04.493
I made a sheikh
in Abu Dhabi an offer
he could not refuse.

1329
01:58:04.828 --> 01:58:07.079
Huh. That's a nice
lady you got there, too.

1330
01:58:07.164 --> 01:58:10.583
Absolutely.
What's happening?
(LAUGHING)

1331
01:58:11.376 --> 01:58:13.586
We got to go, man.
Let's do this.

1332
01:58:13.670 --> 01:58:15.337
Okay, I'll drive.

1333
01:58:15.422 --> 01:58:17.965
In that?
Come on, man,
no way.

1334
01:58:18.049 --> 01:58:20.342
No, no. Not in this.

1335
01:58:20.427 --> 01:58:21.594
In that.

1336
01:58:27.934 --> 01:58:29.477
Are you serious right now?

1337
01:58:30.270 --> 01:58:31.604
Man, this is crazy!

1338
01:58:31.688 --> 01:58:36.275
Yes, I guess that means
there are two in the
Western Hemisphere, huh?

1339
01:58:37.152 --> 01:58:39.487
What's your smart ass
got to say now?

1340
01:58:40.030 --> 01:58:43.449
You know what?
We can always
shine together, baby.

1341
01:58:43.533 --> 01:58:45.910
Get dressed, man,
we got things to do!

1342
01:58:58.340 --> 01:58:59.799
So, where to now?

1343
01:58:59.883 --> 01:59:01.425
I don't know.

1344
01:59:01.510 --> 01:59:03.886
Never been to Madrid.

1345
01:59:03.970 --> 01:59:06.722
I thought you wanted
to go to Tokyo.

1346
01:59:06.807 --> 01:59:08.974
We'll get there.

1347
01:59:09.059 --> 01:59:10.684
Eventually.

1348
02:00:10.036 --> 02:00:11.871
BRIAN: Nice surprise.

1349
02:00:15.458 --> 02:00:17.126
Crazy, right?

1350
02:00:25.343 --> 02:00:28.387
This is the happiest
I've ever seen my sister.

1351
02:00:29.431 --> 02:00:31.432
It's because we're free.

1352
02:00:44.779 --> 02:00:47.031
You know,
I want another shot.

1353
02:00:50.577 --> 02:00:51.577
Yeah?

1354
02:00:53.663 --> 02:00:55.331
Yeah.

1355
02:00:55.415 --> 02:00:57.249
No wagers, nobody else.

1356
02:00:57.334 --> 02:00:59.501
Just you and me,
once and for all.

1357
02:01:06.593 --> 02:01:08.552
You sure you can handle
the disappointment?

1358
02:01:09.429 --> 02:01:10.846
Are you?

1359
02:01:13.141 --> 02:01:15.225
All right, O'Conner.

1360
02:01:15.310 --> 02:01:17.144
Let's see what you got.

1361
02:03:25.690 --> 02:03:30.235
DIPLOMATIC SECURITY
SERVICE HEADQUARTERS -
WASHINGTON, D.C.

1362
02:03:33.281 --> 02:03:34.281
(TYPING)

1363
02:03:45.001 --> 02:03:46.835
You need to look at that.

1364
02:03:50.757 --> 02:03:52.716
Berlin, 3:00 a.m.
This morning.

1365
02:03:52.967 --> 02:03:55.761
A team of drivers
hijacked a military convoy.

1366
02:03:55.845 --> 02:03:57.679
Toretto?
Nope.

1367
02:03:58.681 --> 02:03:59.640
I ain't interested.

1368
02:03:59.724 --> 02:04:02.559
Yes, you are.
Keep looking.

1369
02:04:14.072 --> 02:04:15.906
Do you believe in ghosts?

1370
02:04:21.121 --> 02:04:23.622
THE MOTOR VEHICLE ACTION
SEQUENCES DEPICTED
IN THIS FILM ARE DANGEROUS.

1371
02:04:23.706 --> 02:04:25.791
ALL STUNTS WERE PERFORMED
IN CONTROLLED ENVIRONMENTS

1372
02:04:25.875 --> 02:04:28.001
WITH PROFESSIONALLY TRAINED
STUNT CREWS ON CLOSED ROADS.

1373
02:04:28.086 --> 02:04:30.212
NO ATTEMPTS SHOULD BE MADE
TO DUPLICATE ANY ACTION,

1374
02:04:30.296 --> 02:04:32.881
DRIVING OR CAR PLAY SCENES
HEREIN PORTRAYED.
